<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Kristina P. Sinaga
</span><span id="id1" class="ltx_note ltx_note_frontmatter ltx_thanks_correspondence ltx_role_thanks"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_type">thanks: </span>Corresponding author: Independent Researcher. ORCID: 0009-0000-6184-829X. Email: sinagakristinap@gmail.com. Research interests include federated learning, multi-view clustering, privacy-preserving machine learning, heat kernel methods, quantum field theory applications in machine learning, and distributed intelligent systems.</span></span></span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>Independent Researcher
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_email"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Email: </span><a href="mailto:"><span id="id2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sinagakristinap@gmail.com</span></a>
</span></span></span></span></div>
<div class="ltx_dates">September 19, 2025</div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">In the realm of distributed AI and privacy-focused medical applications, we propose a framework for multi-view clustering that links quantum field theory with federated healthcare analytics. Our method uses heat-kernel coefficients from spectral analysis to convert Euclidean distances into geometry-aware similarity measures, capturing the structure of diverse medical data. We lay this out through the Heat Kernel Distance (HKD) transformation with convergence guarantees. Two algorithms are developed: Heat Kernel-Enhanced Multi-View Fuzzy Clustering (HK-MVFC) for central analysis, and Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Fuzzy Clustering (FedHK-MVFC) for secure, privacy-preserving learning across hospitals using differential privacy and secure aggregation to facilitate HIPAA-compliant collaboration. Tests on synthetic datasets of cardiovascular patients show an 8-12% increase in clustering accuracy, 70% reduced communication, and 98.2% efficiency retention over centralized methods. Validated on 10,000 patient records across two hospitals, it proves useful for collaborative phenotyping involving ECG, cardiac imaging, and behavioral data. Our theoretical contributions include update rules with proven convergence, adaptive view weighting, and privacy-preserving protocols. This presents a new standard for geometry-aware federated learning in healthcare, turning advanced math into workable solutions for analyzing sensitive medical data while ensuring both rigor and clinical relevance.</p>
    
<p id="abstract1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="abstract1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Keywords:</span> Federated learning, Multi-view clustering, Heat kernel methods, Privacy-preserving healthcare, Medical data analysis, Quantum field theory, Distributed machine learning</p>
  
</div>
<div id="id3" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_align_bottom">
    <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:2.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
    <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:2.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
    
<div id="p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="p1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_top">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="p1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:0.0pt;height:24.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"></span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
  
</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The increasing prevalence of heterogeneous data sources has spurred significant interest in multi-view (MV) clustering, wherein a single entity is characterized by multiple distinct feature sets or “views.” In such contexts, traditional clustering methods often fall short, necessitating sophisticated approaches that can effectively integrate complementary information across diverse views while maintaining coherence in the resulting partition. In addition, the rapid evolution of large-scale artificial intelligence (AI) systems - from centralized language models to decentralized, agent-based architectures - has fundamentally shifted how learning is conceptualized and deployed. In these new paradigms, learning must occur not only across heterogeneous data views but across distributed agents, each operating within their own local context, resource constraints, and knowledge representation. This shift demands a theoretical and algorithmic framework that accommodates structural diversity, communication limitations, and the intrinsic geometry of information flow.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this work, we propose a novel soft clustering framework that replaces conventional Euclidean distance (CED) with kernelized geometric measures derived from H-KC – tools rooted in QFT and spectral analysis. By modeling similarity via heat diffusion over data manifolds, our approach provides a richer, geometry-aware mechanism for aggregating and aligning distributed views. Moreover, the theoretical underpinnings from QFT offer a natural interpretation of influence propagation – a notion increasingly relevant in the context of collaborative AI and agent-based systems.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the case of multiple hospitals collaboratively monitoring cardiovascular health through FL – one through ECG signals, another via MRI imaging, others through wearables, EHRs, or genetic data. While CED treats each view as flat and uniform, it fails to capture the curved anatomical structures in imaging or the relational dependencies in medical histories. The HKD, in contrast, models how <span id="S1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">“information”</span> or similarity diffuses across each hospital’s local data manifold—honoring intrinsic structures. This enables the clustering of patients who may appear dissimilar numerically but share underlying physiological patterns across modalities.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Our method enables flexible, privacy-preserving learning across multiple views and agents, with theoretical guarantees and practical scalability. It bridges foundational mathematics with contemporary machine learning (ML) architecture, contributing a unified lens to interpret and design decentralized intelligent systems (DIS). In summary, the contributions of this study include:</p>
<ol id="S1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the era of modular AI, where not only data views but distributed agents must harmonize across diverse sources, we propose a unified theoretical framework bridging MV learning, kernel geometry, and quantum field theory (QFT) to support scalable, interpretable federated learning (FL).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Just as large language models (LLMs) or “LLM-agents” encode semantic geometry in high-dimensional manifolds, this work proposes heat kernel-based soft clustering to capture local geometric structures across decentralized views. In other words, this paper revisits the principles of information diffusion, not only across data views but across distributed agents-drawing connections from classical field theory to the most recent breakthroughs in neural language model.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce a novel centralized clustering algorithms that bridge the Heat Kernel-Enhanced Multi-View Fuzzy Clustering (HK-MVFC).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proposed HK-MVFC algorithm employs H-KC to transform the CED metric into an HKD, enabling more effective capturing of complex relationship between data points and cluster centers across multiple views. Here, HK-MVFC incorporates view-specific weighting factors to balance the contribution of each view and treats feature-specific weights across views are equally important.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We implement the mathematical formulation for federated HK-MVFC, abbreviated as FedHK-MVFC. The federated variant of HK-MVFC employs a parameter synchronization protocol that preserves data privacy.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Literature Review</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we review the relevant literature on federated learning, clustering, and their intersections.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Federated learning (FL) has emerged as a paradigm for collaborative model training across decentralized data sources while preserving privacy <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>. Early works focused on federated averaging (FedAvg) and its variants, addressing communication efficiency and robustness to data heterogeneity. Recent advances include personalization strategies <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>, secure aggregation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>, and applications in healthcare, finance, and IoT.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Clustering algorithms, such as k-means, hierarchical clustering, and fuzzy c-means (FCM) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>, are foundational in unsupervised learning. Multi-view clustering extends these methods to data with multiple feature representations, leveraging complementary information for improved accuracy <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>. Kernel-based approaches, including spectral clustering and kernel k-means, address non-linear relationships and manifold structures <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Distributed clustering integrates clustering algorithms with distributed computing frameworks to scale to large datasets and decentralized environments <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>. Federated clustering combines FL principles with clustering, enabling privacy-preserving unsupervised learning across clients <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>. Existing federated clustering methods often rely on communication-efficient protocols and local model updates, but face challenges in handling heterogeneous data distributions and aligning cluster assignments across clients.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Recent works have explored kernel methods and manifold learning in federated settings <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>, highlighting the importance of geometry-aware similarity measures. However, most approaches use conventional distance metrics and lack theoretical guarantees for convergence and consistency in multi-view, distributed contexts.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Our work builds on these foundations by introducing heat-kernel coefficients and kernelized distances for multi-view federated clustering, bridging quantum field theory concepts with practical distributed learning algorithms.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1 </span>Federated Learning</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Federated learning (FL) enables decentralized model training by aggregating updates from multiple clients, each operating on local data. The core mechanism involves iterative communication between clients and a central server, where clients compute local model updates and the server aggregates these updates to refine the global model. This approach mitigates privacy risks associated with centralized data storage and is particularly suited for sensitive domains such as healthcare, finance, and mobile applications.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Key challenges in FL include handling data heterogeneity, ensuring communication efficiency, and maintaining model convergence. Techniques such as federated averaging (FedAvg) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>, secure aggregation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>, and personalization strategies <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite> have been developed to address these issues. Recent research also explores robust aggregation methods, differential privacy, and federated optimization algorithms to further enhance FL’s scalability and reliability.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In the context of clustering, federated learning introduces additional complexity due to the unsupervised nature of the task and the need to align cluster assignments across clients. Existing federated clustering approaches often rely on communication-efficient protocols and local model updates, but face challenges in managing heterogeneous data distributions and achieving consistent clustering results. Our work builds on these foundations by integrating geometry-aware kernel methods and heat-kernel coefficients to improve clustering performance in federated multi-view settings.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2 </span>Clustering</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Clustering algorithms are central to unsupervised learning, aiming to partition data into groups based on similarity. The classical k-means algorithm assigns each data point to the nearest cluster centroid, minimizing intra-cluster variance. Hierarchical clustering builds nested clusters by either agglomerative (bottom-up) or divisive (top-down) strategies, producing a dendrogram that reveals data structure at multiple scales. Fuzzy c-means (FCM) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> generalizes k-means by allowing each data point to belong to multiple clusters with varying degrees of membership, controlled by a fuzzifier parameter.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Multi-view clustering extends these paradigms to datasets where each sample is described by multiple feature sets (views). By integrating information from different views, multi-view clustering can achieve more robust and accurate partitions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>. Approaches include co-regularization, consensus clustering, and weighted integration, each addressing the challenge of view heterogeneity.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Kernel-based clustering methods, such as spectral clustering and kernel k-means, leverage kernel functions to capture non-linear relationships and manifold structures in data <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>. Spectral clustering uses the eigenvectors of similarity matrices to embed data into a lower-dimensional space before applying conventional clustering. Kernel k-means replaces the Euclidean distance with kernel-induced similarity, enabling clustering in high-dimensional feature spaces.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Recent advances focus on adaptive weighting of views, automatic selection of kernel parameters, and scalable algorithms for large multi-view datasets. Despite progress, challenges remain in handling noisy views, aligning cluster assignments across views, and providing theoretical guarantees for convergence and consistency.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.3 </span>Distributed Clustering</h3>

<div id="S2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Distributed clustering refers to clustering algorithms designed to operate on data that is partitioned across multiple nodes or clients, often in large-scale or privacy-sensitive environments. In such settings, data cannot be centralized due to privacy, bandwidth, or computational constraints. Distributed clustering methods typically fall into two categories: (1) centralized coordination, where a server aggregates local clustering results or model parameters from clients, and (2) decentralized protocols, where clients communicate directly or via peer-to-peer networks to reach consensus.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Federated clustering is a specialized form of distributed clustering that emphasizes privacy preservation and minimal data sharing. In federated clustering, each client computes local cluster assignments or updates based on its own data, and only shares model parameters (such as cluster centroids or membership matrices) with a central server. The server aggregates these updates—using techniques like weighted averaging or secure aggregation—to refine a global clustering model, which is then redistributed to clients for further local updates. Communication-efficient protocols, such as periodic synchronization or compressed updates, are often employed to reduce bandwidth usage and improve scalability.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Key challenges in distributed and federated clustering include handling heterogeneous data distributions, aligning cluster assignments across clients, ensuring convergence, and maintaining privacy. Recent advances leverage kernel methods, consensus algorithms, and adaptive weighting to address these issues, enabling robust clustering in decentralized environments without compromising data privacy.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The evolution of these techniques has led to more sophisticated frameworks that can dynamically adapt to varying data characteristics and client capabilities. For detailed discussions on distributed clustering, refer to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section presents our proposed heat-kernel enhanced multi-view clustering framework. We first establish the mathematical foundations and notation used throughout our formulations, then develop our two novel clustering algorithms: Heat Kernel-Enhanced Multi-View Fuzzy Clustering (HK-MVFC) and its extension, Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Fuzzy Clustering (FedHK-MVFC). Both algorithms are designed to effectively integrate information across heterogeneous data views in (non) distributed mechanisms while leveraging heat-kernel coefficients to enhance representational capacity.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Mathematical Preliminaries and Problem Formulation</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> as a multi-view dataset consisting of <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> separate views, denoted by <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{X^{h}}=\left\{{x_{1}^{h},\ldots,x_{n}^{h}}\right\}_{h=1}^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{X^{h}}=\left\{{x_{1}^{h},\ldots,x_{n}^{h}}\right\}_{h=1}^{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. Each <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}^{h}=\left\{{x_{ij}^{h}}\right\}_{j=1}^{{d_{h}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}^{h}=\left\{{x_{ij}^{h}}\right\}_{j=1}^{{d_{h}}}</annotation></semantics></math> signifies the <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th data point in the <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>-th view, and the total dimensions are such that <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\nolimits_{h=1}^{s}{{d_{h}}=D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\nolimits_{h=1}^{s}{{d_{h}}=D}</annotation></semantics></math>. The data matrix <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is divided into <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> clusters over all <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> views, represented by a global membership matrix <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mu^{*}}={\left[{\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right]_{n\times c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mu^{*}}={\left[{\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right]_{n\times c}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where each element <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{ik}^{*}\in\left[{0,1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{ik}^{*}\in\left[{0,1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> adheres to the rule <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\nolimits_{k=1}^{c}{\mu_{ik}^{*}=1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\nolimits_{k=1}^{c}{\mu_{ik}^{*}=1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The weights of the views are given by the vector <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v={\left[{{v_{h}}}\right]_{1\times s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v={\left[{{v_{h}}}\right]_{1\times s}}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{v_{h}}\in\left[{0,1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{v_{h}}\in\left[{0,1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> and ensuring <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\nolimits_{h=1}^{s}{{v_{h}}=1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\nolimits_{h=1}^{s}{{v_{h}}=1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Cluster centroids in each view <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> are indicated by <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{A^{h}}={\left[{a_{kj}^{h}}\right]_{c\times{d_{h}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{A^{h}}={\left[{a_{kj}^{h}}\right]_{c\times{d_{h}}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Heat-Kernel Coefficients</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Central to our approach is the formulation of heat-kernel coefficients (H-KC), which enables the transformation of Euclidean distance in the original feature space to an exponential kernel distance. For the <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th feature in the <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>-th view, we define H-KC <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{ij}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{ij}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> using two alternative estimators:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{ij}^{h}=\frac{{x_{ij}^{h}-\mathop{\min}\limits_{1\leq i\leq n}\left({x_{ij}^{h}}\right)}}{{\mathop{\max}\limits_{1\leq i\leq n}\left({x_{ij}^{h}}\right)-\mathop{\min}\limits_{1\leq i\leq n}\left({x_{ij}^{h}}\right)}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">min</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">max</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">min</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{ij}^{h}=\frac{{x_{ij}^{h}-\mathop{\min}\limits_{1\leq i\leq n}\left({x_{ij}^{h}}\right)}}{{\mathop{\max}\limits_{1\leq i\leq n}\left({x_{ij}^{h}}\right)-\mathop{\min}\limits_{1\leq i\leq n}\left({x_{ij}^{h}}\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Note:</span> To ensure numerical stability, a small constant <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is added to the denominator. If all feature values are identical, <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max=\min" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max=\min</annotation></semantics></math>, and the denominator becomes <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> to avoid division by zero.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">and</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{ij}^{h}=\left|{x_{ij}^{h}-{{\bar{x}}^{h}}}\right|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{ij}^{h}=\left|{x_{ij}^{h}-{{\bar{x}}^{h}}}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{x}^{h}={1\mathord{\left/{\vphantom{1n}}\right.\kern-1.2pt}n}\sum\nolimits_{i=1}^{n}{x_{ij}^{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.380em;" width="0.380em"><mi>/</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{x}^{h}={1\mathord{\left/{\vphantom{1n}}\right.\kern-1.2pt}n}\sum\nolimits_{i=1}^{n}{x_{ij}^{h}}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the mean value of the <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th feature in view <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Conventional Fuzzy C-Means in Multi-View Context</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The standard fuzzy c-means (FCM) algorithm minimizes the following objective function:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{J_{FCM}}\left({U,V}\right)=\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c}{\mu_{ik}^{m}}}\sum\limits_{j=1}^{d}{{{\left({{x_{ij}}-{a_{kj}}}\right)}^{2}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{J_{FCM}}\left({U,V}\right)=\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c}{\mu_{ik}^{m}}}\sum\limits_{j=1}^{d}{{{\left({{x_{ij}}-{a_{kj}}}\right)}^{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> is the fuzzifier parameter controlling the degree of fuzziness in the resulting partitions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In a multi-view setting, conventional FCM faces limitations when attempting to derive unified patterns from heterogeneous data sources. These limitations stem from its reliance on the Euclidean distance metric, which fails to capture non-linear relationships and cannot effectively balance contributions from views of varying dimensionality, scale, and noise characteristics.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4 </span>Heat Kernel-Enhanced Multi-View Fuzzy Clustering</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To address the challenges of clustering heterogeneous multi-view data, we propose the Heat Kernel-Enhanced Multi-View Fuzzy Clustering (HK-MVFC) algorithm. This approach integrates heat-kernel coefficients into a fuzzy clustering framework, enabling more effective capture of complex relationships between data points and cluster centers across multiple views.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The foundation of our approach is the transformation of conventional Euclidean distance metrics into exponential kernel distances. To achieve this, we introduce a novel Kernel Euclidean Distance (KED) formulation:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\rm{KE}}{{\rm{D}}_{1}}\left({x_{ij}^{h},a_{kj}^{h}}\right)=\exp\left({-\sum\limits_{j=1}^{{d_{h}}}{\delta_{ij}^{h}{{\left({x_{ij}^{h}-a_{kj}^{h}}\right)}^{2}}}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>KED</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></munderover><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm{KE}}{{\rm{D}}_{1}}\left({x_{ij}^{h},a_{kj}^{h}}\right)=\exp\left({-\sum\limits_{j=1}^{{d_{h}}}{\delta_{ij}^{h}{{\left({x_{ij}^{h}-a_{kj}^{h}}\right)}^{2}}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In Eq. <a href="#S3.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ 3.4 Heat Kernel-Enhanced Multi-View Fuzzy Clustering ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, the H-KC acts as adaptive weighting factors, enabling the algorithm to effectively balance between local and global feature importance. This formulation maps distances to the range <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[{0,1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[{0,1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, with values approaching 1 indicating high similarity between data points and cluster centers.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For clustering purposes, we require a dissimilarity measure that approaches zero for identical points. Therefore, we normalize <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm{KE}}{{\rm{D}}_{1}}\left({x_{ij}^{h},a_{kj}^{h}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>KED</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm{KE}}{{\rm{D}}_{1}}\left({x_{ij}^{h},a_{kj}^{h}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\rm{KE}}{{\rm{D}}_{2}}\left({x_{ij}^{h},a_{kj}^{h}}\right)=1-\exp\left({-\sum\limits_{j=1}^{{d_{h}}}{\delta_{ij}^{h}{{\left({x_{ij}^{h}-a_{kj}^{h}}\right)}^{2}}}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>KED</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></munderover><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm{KE}}{{\rm{D}}_{2}}\left({x_{ij}^{h},a_{kj}^{h}}\right)=1-\exp\left({-\sum\limits_{j=1}^{{d_{h}}}{\delta_{ij}^{h}{{\left({x_{ij}^{h}-a_{kj}^{h}}\right)}^{2}}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">We denote <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm{KE}}{{\rm{D}}_{2}}\left({x_{ij}^{h},a_{kj}^{h}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>KED</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm{KE}}{{\rm{D}}_{2}}\left({x_{ij}^{h},a_{kj}^{h}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> for notational simplicity in subsequent formulations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Building on the kernel distance transformation, we formulate the HK-MVFC objective function as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{J_{HK-MVFC}}\left({V,U,A}\right)=\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s}{v_{h}^{\alpha}}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}}}d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{J_{HK-MVFC}}\left({V,U,A}\right)=\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s}{v_{h}^{\alpha}}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}}}d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Subject to:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c}{\mu_{ik}^{*}=1},{\rm{}}\mu_{ik}^{*}\in\left[{0,1}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c}{\mu_{ik}^{*}=1},{\rm{}}\mu_{ik}^{*}\in\left[{0,1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s}{{v_{h}}=1,{\rm{}}{v_{h}}\in\left[{0,1}\right]}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s}{{v_{h}}=1,{\rm{}}{v_{h}}\in\left[{0,1}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p12.1" class="ltx_p">The exponent parameter <math id="S3.SS4.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> of our proposed HK-MVFC in Eq. <a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ 3.4 Heat Kernel-Enhanced Multi-View Fuzzy Clustering ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> controls the influence of view weights, with larger values increasing the contrast between different views’ contributions. Here, we set <math id="S3.SS4.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, a user-defined parameter that adjusts the real-world problem needs. And the fuzzifier <math id="S3.SS4.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> determines the fuzziness of the resulting partition.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p13.1" class="ltx_p">A critical aspect of our approach is the use of a unified membership matrix <math id="S3.SS4.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=\left[{\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=\left[{\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> across all views. Unlike approaches that compute separate memberships for each view and subsequently merge them, HK-MVFC enforces consistency across views from the outset, resulting in a more coherent clustering structure.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.5 </span>Optimization Framework: HK-MVFC</h3>

<div id="S3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The objective function of proposed HK-MVFC in Eq. <a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ 3.4 Heat Kernel-Enhanced Multi-View Fuzzy Clustering ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> cannot be minimized directly due to its non-convex nature. We therefore employ an alternating optimization approach, iteratively updating the membership matrix <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, the view weights <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, and the cluster centers <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To derive the update rules, we construct the Lagrangian of Eq. <a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ 3.4 Heat Kernel-Enhanced Multi-View Fuzzy Clustering ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> in the following way</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{{\tilde{J}}_{HK-MVFC}}={J_{HK-MVFC}}\left({V,U,A}\right)+\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{{\lambda_{1i}}}\left({\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c}{\mu_{ik}^{*}-1}}\right)+{\lambda_{2}}\left({\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s}{{v_{h}}-1}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{{\tilde{J}}_{HK-MVFC}}={J_{HK-MVFC}}\left({V,U,A}\right)+\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{{\lambda_{1i}}}\left({\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c}{\mu_{ik}^{*}-1}}\right)+{\lambda_{2}}\left({\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s}{{v_{h}}-1}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are Lagrange multipliers enforcing the normalization constraints.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(HK-MVFC Update Rules)<span id="Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The necessary conditions for minimizing the objective function <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{HK-MVFC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{HK-MVFC}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ 3.4 Heat Kernel-Enhanced Multi-View Fuzzy Clustering ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> yield the following update rules:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{ik}^{*}=\frac{{{{\left({\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s}{v_{h}^{\alpha}d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h}}}\right)}^{-{{\left({m-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}}}{{\sum\limits_{k^{\prime}=1}^{c}{{{\left({\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s}{v_{h}^{\alpha}d_{\exp\left({ik^{\prime},j}\right)}^{h}}}\right)}^{-{{\left({m-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{ik}^{*}=\frac{{{{\left({\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s}{v_{h}^{\alpha}d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h}}}\right)}^{-{{\left({m-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}}}{{\sum\limits_{k^{\prime}=1}^{c}{{{\left({\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s}{v_{h}^{\alpha}d_{\exp\left({ik^{\prime},j}\right)}^{h}}}\right)}^{-{{\left({m-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{kj}^{h}=\frac{{\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}v_{h}^{\alpha}\exp\left({-\delta_{ij}^{h}{{\left\|{x_{i}^{h}-a_{k}^{h}}\right\|}^{2}}}\right)}}}{{\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}v_{h}^{\alpha}\exp\left({-\delta_{ij}^{h}{{\left\|{x_{i}^{h}-a_{k}^{h}}\right\|}^{2}}}\right)}}}x_{ij}^{h}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{kj}^{h}=\frac{{\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}v_{h}^{\alpha}\exp\left({-\delta_{ij}^{h}{{\left\|{x_{i}^{h}-a_{k}^{h}}\right\|}^{2}}}\right)}}}{{\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}v_{h}^{\alpha}\exp\left({-\delta_{ij}^{h}{{\left\|{x_{i}^{h}-a_{k}^{h}}\right\|}^{2}}}\right)}}}x_{ij}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{v_{h}}=\frac{{{{\left({\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h}}}}\right)}^{-{{\left({\alpha-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}}}{{\sum\limits_{h^{\prime}=1}^{s}{{{\left({\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h^{\prime}}}}}\right)}^{-{{\left({\alpha-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{v_{h}}=\frac{{{{\left({\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h}}}}\right)}^{-{{\left({\alpha-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}}}{{\sum\limits_{h^{\prime}=1}^{s}{{{\left({\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h^{\prime}}}}}\right)}^{-{{\left({\alpha-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We start by formulating the update equation for the membership coefficients <math id="S3.SS5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{ik}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{ik}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is done by computing the partial derivative of the Lagrangian presented in Eq. <a href="#S3.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ 3.5 Optimization Framework: HK-MVFC ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> with respect to <math id="S3.SS5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{ik}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{ik}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{{\tilde{\partial}{J_{HK-MVFC}}}}{{\partial\mu_{ik}^{*}}}=m{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)^{m-1}}\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s}{v_{h}^{\alpha}}d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h}+{\lambda_{1i}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>∂</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{{\tilde{\partial}{J_{HK-MVFC}}}}{{\partial\mu_{ik}^{*}}}=m{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)^{m-1}}\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s}{v_{h}^{\alpha}}d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h}+{\lambda_{1i}}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Rightarrow\mu_{ik}^{*}={\left({-\frac{{{\lambda_{1i}}}}{m}}\right)^{{{\left({m-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}{\left({\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s}{v_{h}^{\alpha}d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h}}}\right)^{-{{\left({m-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Rightarrow\mu_{ik}^{*}={\left({-\frac{{{\lambda_{1i}}}}{m}}\right)^{{{\left({m-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}{\left({\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s}{v_{h}^{\alpha}d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h}}}\right)^{-{{\left({m-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS5.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">By imposing the condition <math id="S3.SS5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\nolimits_{k=1}^{c}{\mu_{ik}^{*}=1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\nolimits_{k=1}^{c}{\mu_{ik}^{*}=1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c}{{{\left({-\frac{{{\lambda_{1i}}}}{m}}\right)}^{{{\left({m-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}}{\left({\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s}{v_{h}^{\alpha}d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h}}}\right)^{-{{\left({m-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c}{{{\left({-\frac{{{\lambda_{1i}}}}{m}}\right)}^{{{\left({m-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}}{\left({\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s}{v_{h}^{\alpha}d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h}}}\right)^{-{{\left({m-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Rightarrow{\left({-\frac{{{\lambda_{1i}}}}{m}}\right)^{{{\left({m-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}=\frac{1}{{\sum\limits_{k^{\prime}=1}^{c}{{{\left({\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s}{v_{h}^{\alpha}d_{\exp\left({ik^{\prime},j}\right)}^{h}}}\right)}^{-{{\left({m-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msup><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Rightarrow{\left({-\frac{{{\lambda_{1i}}}}{m}}\right)^{{{\left({m-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}=\frac{1}{{\sum\limits_{k^{\prime}=1}^{c}{{{\left({\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s}{v_{h}^{\alpha}d_{\exp\left({ik^{\prime},j}\right)}^{h}}}\right)}^{-{{\left({m-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS5.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting Eq. <a href="#S3.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.5 Optimization Framework: HK-MVFC ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> into Eq. <a href="#S3.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.5 Optimization Framework: HK-MVFC ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> yields Eq. <a href="#S3.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ Theorem 1 (HK-MVFC Update Rules). ‣ 3.5 Optimization Framework: HK-MVFC ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS5.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">To find the cluster centers <math id="S3.SS5.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{kj}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{kj}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, we differentiate the HK-MVFC objective in Eq. <a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ 3.4 Heat Kernel-Enhanced Multi-View Fuzzy Clustering ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> with respect to <math id="S3.SS5.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{kj}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{kj}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{{\partial{J_{HK-MVFC}}}}{{\partial a_{kj}^{h}}}=v_{h}^{\alpha}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}}\frac{{\partial d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h}}}{{\partial a_{kj}^{h}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{{\partial{J_{HK-MVFC}}}}{{\partial a_{kj}^{h}}}=v_{h}^{\alpha}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}}\frac{{\partial d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h}}}{{\partial a_{kj}^{h}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=v_{h}^{\alpha}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}}\frac{\partial}{{\partial a_{kj}^{h}}}\left\{{1-\exp\left({-\sum\limits_{j=1}^{{d_{h}}}{\delta_{ij}^{h}{{\left({x_{ij}^{h}-a_{kj}^{h}}\right)}^{2}}}}\right)}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=v_{h}^{\alpha}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}}\frac{\partial}{{\partial a_{kj}^{h}}}\left\{{1-\exp\left({-\sum\limits_{j=1}^{{d_{h}}}{\delta_{ij}^{h}{{\left({x_{ij}^{h}-a_{kj}^{h}}\right)}^{2}}}}\right)}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-v_{h}^{\alpha}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}}\frac{\partial}{{\partial a_{kj}^{h}}}\exp\left({-\sum\limits_{j=1}^{{d_{h}}}{\delta_{ij}^{h}{{\left({x_{ij}^{h}-a_{kj}^{h}}\right)}^{2}}}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-v_{h}^{\alpha}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}}\frac{\partial}{{\partial a_{kj}^{h}}}\exp\left({-\sum\limits_{j=1}^{{d_{h}}}{\delta_{ij}^{h}{{\left({x_{ij}^{h}-a_{kj}^{h}}\right)}^{2}}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=2\delta_{ij}^{h}v_{h}^{\alpha}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}\exp\left({-\sum\limits_{j=1}^{{d_{h}}}{\delta_{ij}^{h}{{\left({x_{ij}^{h}-a_{kj}^{h}}\right)}^{2}}}}\right)}\left({x_{ij}^{h}-a_{kj}^{h}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\delta_{ij}^{h}v_{h}^{\alpha}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}\exp\left({-\sum\limits_{j=1}^{{d_{h}}}{\delta_{ij}^{h}{{\left({x_{ij}^{h}-a_{kj}^{h}}\right)}^{2}}}}\right)}\left({x_{ij}^{h}-a_{kj}^{h}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS5.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Setting the derivative in Eq. <a href="#S3.E18" title="Equation 18 ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.5 Optimization Framework: HK-MVFC ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> to zero and solving for <math id="S3.SS5.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{kj}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{kj}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> gives Eq. <a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Theorem 1 (HK-MVFC Update Rules). ‣ 3.5 Optimization Framework: HK-MVFC ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>. Then, we compute the partial derivative of the Lagrangian in Eq. <a href="#S3.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ 3.5 Optimization Framework: HK-MVFC ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> with respect to <math id="S3.SS5.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{v_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{v_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math> to update the weight function for views <math id="S3.SS5.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{v_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{v_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{{\partial{{\tilde{J}}_{HK-MVFC}}}}{{\partial{v_{h}}}}=\alpha v_{h}^{\alpha-1}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}}}d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h}+{\lambda_{2}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{{\partial{{\tilde{J}}_{HK-MVFC}}}}{{\partial{v_{h}}}}=\alpha v_{h}^{\alpha-1}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}}}d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h}+{\lambda_{2}}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Rightarrow{v_{h}}={\left({-\frac{{{\lambda_{2}}}}{\alpha}}\right)^{{{\left({\alpha-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}{\left({\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h}}}}\right)^{-{{\left({\alpha-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Rightarrow{v_{h}}={\left({-\frac{{{\lambda_{2}}}}{\alpha}}\right)^{{{\left({\alpha-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}{\left({\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c}{{{\left({\mu_{ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}d_{\exp\left({ik,j}\right)}^{h}}}}\right)^{-{{\left({\alpha-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS5.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">From constraint <math id="S3.SS5.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\nolimits_{h=1}^{s}{{v_{h}}=1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\nolimits_{h=1}^{s}{{v_{h}}=1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we derive Eq. <a href="#S3.E20" title="Equation 20 ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.5 Optimization Framework: HK-MVFC ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.6 </span>Theoretical Insights</h3>

<div id="S3.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Several important theoretical properties of the HK-MVFC algorithm warrant emphasis. The algorithm exhibits a consistency property where reducing intra-cluster distances within a view while increasing inter-cluster distances across different views preserves the clustering outcome. This property ensures stable performance even with heterogeneous data distributions, which is particularly crucial in multi-view scenarios where individual views may exhibit varying degrees of noise and signal quality.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The update rule for view weights in Eq. <a href="#S3.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Theorem 1 (HK-MVFC Update Rules). ‣ 3.5 Optimization Framework: HK-MVFC ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> demonstrates an adaptive weighting mechanism that assigns higher weights to views with smaller intra-cluster distances, effectively prioritizing more informative views during the clustering process. The parameter <math id="S3.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> controls the degree of contrast between view weights, with larger values increasing the differentiation between high-quality and low-quality views. This adaptive behavior enables the algorithm to automatically adjust to the relative informativeness of different data modalities without requiring manual tuning of view contributions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The heat-kernel coefficients <math id="S3.SS6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{ij}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{ij}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> provide a sophisticated mechanism for adapting to the local geometry of the data in each view. Unlike conventional Euclidean distance metrics that assume uniform data distributions, these coefficients capture the intrinsic manifold structure of the data, enabling the algorithm to identify complex cluster structures that may be obscured when using standard distance measures. This geometric sensitivity is particularly valuable when dealing with non-linear cluster boundaries and varying cluster densities across different views.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.7 </span>HK-MVFC Algorithm</h3>

<div id="S3.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm HK-MVFC provides a detailed implementation of the HK-MVFC in Eq. <a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ 3.4 Heat Kernel-Enhanced Multi-View Fuzzy Clustering ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> approach. The algorithm operates by alternately updating the membership matrix, cluster centers, and view weights until convergence.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Heat Kernel-Enhanced Multi-View Fuzzy Clustering (HK-MVFC)</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Multi-view dataset <math id="alg1.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\{X^{h}\}_{h=1}^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\{X^{h}\}_{h=1}^{s}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="alg1.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{h}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{h}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Number of clusters <math id="alg1.l0a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, fuzzifier <math id="alg1.l0a.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, view weight exponent <math id="alg1.l0a.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l0b" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Convergence threshold <math id="alg1.l0b.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, maximum iterations <math id="alg1.l0b.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{max}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l0c" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Membership matrix <math id="alg1.l0c.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{*}\in[0,1]_{n\times c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{*}\in[0,1]_{n\times c}</annotation></semantics></math>, cluster centers <math id="alg1.l0c.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A^{h}\}_{h=1}^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A^{h}\}_{h=1}^{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, view weights <math id="alg1.l0c.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in[0,1]_{1\times s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in[0,1]_{1\times s}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Initialization:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{h^{(0)}}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{h^{(0)}}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Initialize cluster centers using k-means++ or random initialization

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{(0)}\leftarrow[1/s,1/s,\ldots,1/s]^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{(0)}\leftarrow[1/s,1/s,\ldots,1/s]^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> {Equal view weights}

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">repeat</span>


</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leftarrow t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow t+1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">// Heat-Kernel Coefficient Computation</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
                Compute <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{ij}^{h^{(t)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{ij}^{h^{(t)}}</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. <a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ 3.2 Heat-Kernel Coefficients ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> or <a href="#S3.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ 3.2 Heat-Kernel Coefficients ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">// Membership Matrix Update</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
              
              
               Update <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu_{ik}^{*^{(t)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{ik}^{*^{(t)}}</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. <a href="#S3.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ Theorem 1 (HK-MVFC Update Rules). ‣ 3.5 Optimization Framework: HK-MVFC ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">// Cluster Centers Update</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
              
              
               Update <math id="alg1.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{kj}^{h^{(t)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{kj}^{h^{(t)}}</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. <a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Theorem 1 (HK-MVFC Update Rules). ‣ 3.5 Optimization Framework: HK-MVFC ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">21:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">// View Weights Update</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">22:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">23:</span>
              
              
               Update <math id="alg1.l23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{h}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{h}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. <a href="#S3.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Theorem 1 (HK-MVFC Update Rules). ‣ 3.5 Optimization Framework: HK-MVFC ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">24:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l24.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">25:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l25.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">// Convergence Check</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">26:</span>
              
              
              Compute the objective function <math id="alg1.l26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{HK-MVFC}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{HK-MVFC}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. <a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ 3.4 Heat Kernel-Enhanced Multi-View Fuzzy Clustering ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l27" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">27:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta J\leftarrow|J_{HK-MVFC}^{(t)}-J_{HK-MVFC}^{(t-1)}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta J\leftarrow|J_{HK-MVFC}^{(t)}-J_{HK-MVFC}^{(t-1)}|</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l28" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">28:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l28.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">until</span> <math id="alg1.l28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta J&lt;\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta J&lt;\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l28.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">or</span> <math id="alg1.l28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{max}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l29" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">29:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l29.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="alg1.l29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="U^{*^{(t)}},\quad\{A^{h^{(t)}}\}_{h=1}^{s},\quad V^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{*^{(t)}},\quad\{A^{h^{(t)}}\}_{h=1}^{s},\quad V^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.8 </span>Computational Complexity of HK-MVFC</h3>

<div id="S3.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The computational complexity of the HK-MVFC algorithm is determined by several key parameters: the number of data points <math id="S3.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, the dimensionality of view <math id="S3.SS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> denoted as <math id="S3.SS8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, the total number of views <math id="S3.SS8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, and the number of clusters <math id="S3.SS8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. A detailed analysis of each computational component reveals the following complexity characteristics.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS8.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The computation of heat-kernel coefficients <math id="S3.SS8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{ij}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{ij}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> using either Eq. <a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ 3.2 Heat-Kernel Coefficients ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> or <a href="#S3.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ 3.2 Heat-Kernel Coefficients ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> represents the initial computational overhead. For each view, this calculation requires <math id="S3.SS8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(nd_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(nd_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> operations across all <math id="S3.SS8.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> data points. When extended across all <math id="S3.SS8.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> views, the total complexity for heat-kernel coefficient computation becomes <math id="S3.SS8.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(nsd_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(nsd_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> per iteration.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS8.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS8.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The membership matrix update procedure, as defined in Eq. <a href="#S3.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ Theorem 1 (HK-MVFC Update Rules). ‣ 3.5 Optimization Framework: HK-MVFC ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, constitutes the most computationally intensive component of the algorithm. This step requires computing exponential kernel distances between each data point and all cluster centers across all views, resulting in <math id="S3.SS8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(ncd_{h}s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(ncd_{h}s)</annotation></semantics></math> operations. The subsequent normalization step, which ensures that membership values sum to unity for each data point, introduces an additional <math id="S3.SS8.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(nc^{2}s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(nc^{2}s)</annotation></semantics></math> complexity term.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS8.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS8.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Cluster center updates via Eq. <a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Theorem 1 (HK-MVFC Update Rules). ‣ 3.5 Optimization Framework: HK-MVFC ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> involve weighted averaging operations over all data points, where the weights are determined by membership values and exponential terms. The computation of exponential terms requires <math id="S3.SS8.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(ncd_{h}s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(ncd_{h}s)</annotation></semantics></math> operations, while the weighted averaging step contributes <math id="S3.SS8.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(ncd_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(ncd_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> complexity. The view weight update mechanism, as specified in Eq. <a href="#S3.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Theorem 1 (HK-MVFC Update Rules). ‣ 3.5 Optimization Framework: HK-MVFC ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, aggregates clustering costs across all data points and clusters, yielding a computational complexity of <math id="S3.SS8.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(ncs)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(ncs)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS8.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS8.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Combining all computational components, the overall per-iteration complexity is expressed as <math id="S3.SS8.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(nsd_{h}+ncd_{h}s+nc^{2}s+ncd_{h}+ncs)=O(ncd_{h}s+nc^{2}s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(nsd_{h}+ncd_{h}s+nc^{2}s+ncd_{h}+ncs)=O(ncd_{h}s+nc^{2}s)</annotation></semantics></math>. For typical scenarios where the dimensionality significantly exceeds the number of clusters <math id="S3.SS8.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d_{h}\gg c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>≫</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d_{h}\gg c)</annotation></semantics></math> and assuming balanced view dimensionalities across all views, this complexity simplifies to <math id="S3.SS8.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(ncd_{max}s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(ncd_{max}s)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS8.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{max}=\max_{h}d_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{max}=\max_{h}d_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the maximum dimensionality among all views.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS8.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS8.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Empirical analysis demonstrates that the HK-MVFC algorithm typically achieves convergence within <math id="S3.SS8.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=15-25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=15-25</annotation></semantics></math> iterations, depending on data characteristics and initialization quality. Consequently, the total computational complexity becomes <math id="S3.SS8.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(Tncd_{max}s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(Tncd_{max}s)</annotation></semantics></math>, which exhibits favorable linear scaling properties with respect to dataset size and the number of views. This computational efficiency, combined with the algorithm’s superior clustering performance, makes HK-MVFC well-suited for large-scale multi-view clustering applications.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Federated HK-MVFC </h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To implement HK-MVFC within a federated setting, we must reformulate the objective function for distributed optimization across multiple clients while preserving data privacy and ensuring convergence guarantees. Let <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}=\{1,2,\ldots,M\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=\{1,2,\ldots,M\}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> participating clients, where each client <math id="S4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> maintains a local multi-view dataset <math id="S4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{[\ell]}=\{X_{[\ell]}^{h}\}_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{[\ell]}=\{X_{[\ell]}^{h}\}_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> with potentially heterogeneous view compositions and sample distributions. Here, <math id="S4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(\ell)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the number of views for client <math id="S4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, and may vary across clients, reflecting the possibility that each client possesses a different number of data views.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The federated formulation introduces several theoretical challenges: (1) maintaining global clustering coherence while respecting local data sovereignty, (2) handling statistical heterogeneity across client datasets, and (3) ensuring that heat-kernel coefficients computed locally preserve the global geometric structure. Our proposed framework addresses these challenges by enabling decentralized optimization, adaptive aggregation, and privacy-preserving coordination among clients, ensuring both robust clustering and data confidentiality.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Problem Formulation</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a federated setting with <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> clients, where each client <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> holds <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(\ell)</annotation></semantics></math> views of local data. For client <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>-th view is denoted as <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{[\ell]}^{h}=\{x_{[\ell]i}^{h}\}_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{[\ell]}^{h}=\{x_{[\ell]i}^{h}\}_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{[\ell]i}^{h}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{[\ell]}^{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{[\ell]i}^{h}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{[\ell]}^{h}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th sample in view <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the complete multi-view dataset for client <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{[\ell]}=\{X_{[\ell]}^{1},X_{[\ell]}^{2},\ldots,X_{[\ell]}^{s(\ell)}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{[\ell]}=\{X_{[\ell]}^{1},X_{[\ell]}^{2},\ldots,X_{[\ell]}^{s(\ell)}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{[\ell]}^{h}\in\mathbb{R}^{n(\ell)\times d_{[\ell]}^{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{[\ell]}^{h}\in\mathbb{R}^{n(\ell)\times d_{[\ell]}^{h}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Each client possesses the same feature set for each view, but the number of samples per view may vary across clients. Definitions include:</p>
<ul id="S4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n(\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n(\ell)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the quantity of data samples possessed by client <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(\ell)</annotation></semantics></math> refers to the number of views client <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> holds</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\left[\ell\right]}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\left[\ell\right]}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> signifies the dimensionality of the <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>-th view for client <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Federated KED</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We assume that while participating clients may contribute varying numbers of samples, each data view shares the same set of features. Thus, the actual or expected cluster formations of multi-view datasets managed by the clients are not required to be identical. This implies that clients can handle multi-view datasets with differing quantities of clusters. By considering this, we can extend <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{KED}_{2}\left({x_{ij}^{h},a_{kj}^{h}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>KED</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{KED}_{2}\left({x_{ij}^{h},a_{kj}^{h}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <a href="#S3.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ 3.4 Heat Kernel-Enhanced Multi-View Fuzzy Clustering ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> to a federated context, referred to as federated kernel Euclidean distance (FKED). The FKED is formulated as follows</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S4.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{FKED}\left(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h}\right)=1-\exp\left(-\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}\sum_{j=1}^{d_{[\ell]}^{h}}\delta_{[\ell]ij}^{h}\left(x_{[\ell]ij}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}\right)^{2}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>FKED</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></munderover><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FKED}\left(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h}\right)=1-\exp\left(-\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}\sum_{j=1}^{d_{[\ell]}^{h}}\delta_{[\ell]ij}^{h}\left(x_{[\ell]ij}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}\right)^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the H-KC linked to the <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>-th client, and <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\ell)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the total clusters managed by client <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\ell)</annotation></semantics></math> may differ across clients, reflecting the flexibility of federated learning to accommodate heterogeneous data distributions and local clustering requirements.
This allows each client to select an appropriate number of clusters based on its own data characteristics, which is crucial for robust and personalized federated analysis.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Federated Heat-Kernel Coefficients</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We focus on developing federated heat-kernel coefficients (FedH-KC), which are computed locally by each client to transform feature distances into privacy-preserving exponential kernel measures tailored to the federated setting. For the <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th feature in view <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, we define FedH-KC <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> using two distinct estimators.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S4.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FedH-KC}=\delta_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}=\frac{x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}-\min_{1\leq i\leq n(\ell)}\left(x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}\right)}{\max_{1\leq i\leq n(\ell)}\left(x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}\right)-\min_{1\leq i\leq n(\ell)}\left(x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}\right)+\epsilon}\qquad\forall j,h,\ell" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>FedH-KC</mtext><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FedH-KC}=\delta_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}=\frac{x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}-\min_{1\leq i\leq n(\ell)}\left(x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}\right)}{\max_{1\leq i\leq n(\ell)}\left(x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}\right)-\min_{1\leq i\leq n(\ell)}\left(x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}\right)+\epsilon}\qquad\forall j,h,\ell</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> prevents division by zero when features have identical values. This normalizes features within each view for consistent distance calculations across clients with different data distributions. and</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S4.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FedH-KC}=\delta_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}=\left|{x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}-{{\bar{x}}_{\left[\ell\right]j}}^{h}}\right|\qquad\forall j,h,\ell" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>FedH-KC</mtext><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mmultiscripts><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FedH-KC}=\delta_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}=\left|{x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}-{{\bar{x}}_{\left[\ell\right]j}}^{h}}\right|\qquad\forall j,h,\ell</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{x}_{[\ell]j}^{h}=\frac{1}{n(\ell)}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}x_{[\ell]ij}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{x}_{[\ell]j}^{h}=\frac{1}{n(\ell)}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}x_{[\ell]ij}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the mean value of the <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th feature in view <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> for client <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, harmonizing with the centralized case notation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.4 </span>The Objective Function</h3>

<div id="S4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In a federated setting with <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> clients, we connect FedHK-MVFC and FKED before introducing the main objective function. The FedHK-MVFC algorithm extends the centralized HK-MVFC by distributing computation across clients while retaining heat kernel-enhanced distance properties. Each client <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> holds local multi-view data <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{[\ell]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{[\ell]}</annotation></semantics></math> and computes local heat-kernel coefficients <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{[\ell]ij}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{[\ell]ij}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, converting Euclidean distances into geometry-aware similarities. Through the FKED, local client computations align with the federated objective. For client <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, the local goal reflects the centralized HK-MVFC structure tailored to client-specific data, with local federated kernel distance <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\exp([\ell],ik,j)}^{h}=\text{FKED}\left(x_{[\ell]ij}^{h},a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>FKED</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\exp([\ell],ik,j)}^{h}=\text{FKED}\left(x_{[\ell]ij}^{h},a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> maintaining geometric properties within distributed processing. This federated system combines local results for global clustering coherence without losing data locality. On this basis, the FedHK-MVFC objective for client <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S4.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{FedHK-MVFC}^{\ell}(V,{U^{*}},A)=\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s\left(\ell\right)}{v_{\left[\ell\right]h}^{\alpha}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n\left(\ell\right)}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c\left(\ell\right)}{{{\left({\mu_{\left[\ell\right]ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}{\rm{FKED}}\left({x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h},a_{\left[\ell\right]kj}^{h}}\right)}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>FKED</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{FedHK-MVFC}^{\ell}(V,{U^{*}},A)=\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s\left(\ell\right)}{v_{\left[\ell\right]h}^{\alpha}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n\left(\ell\right)}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c\left(\ell\right)}{{{\left({\mu_{\left[\ell\right]ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}{\rm{FKED}}\left({x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h},a_{\left[\ell\right]kj}^{h}}\right)}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Subject to standard fuzzy clustering constraints:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S4.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}{\mu_{\left[\ell\right]ik}^{*}=1},{\rm{}}\mu_{\left[\ell\right]ik}^{*}\in\left[{0,1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}{\mu_{\left[\ell\right]ik}^{*}=1},{\rm{}}\mu_{\left[\ell\right]ik}^{*}\in\left[{0,1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s\left(\ell\right)}{{v_{\left[\ell\right]h}}=1,{\rm{}}{v_{\left[\ell\right]h}}\in\left[{0,1}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s\left(\ell\right)}{{v_{\left[\ell\right]h}}=1,{\rm{}}{v_{\left[\ell\right]h}}\in\left[{0,1}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.5 </span>Optimization Framework</h3>

<div id="S4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Due to the non-convex nature of the FedHK-MVFC objective function in Eq. <a href="#S4.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ 4.4 The Objective Function ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>, direct minimization is not feasible. We employ an alternating optimization strategy that iteratively updates the membership matrix <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, view weights <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, and cluster centers <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> until convergence.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To derive the update rules, we formulate the Lagrangian incorporating the normalization constraints:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S4.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\tilde{J}_{FedHK-MVFC}^{\ell}&amp;=J_{FedHK-MVFC}^{\ell}(V,{U^{*}},A)\\
&amp;\quad+\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}{\lambda_{1i}}\left(\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}{\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}-1}\right)+{\lambda_{2}}\left(\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}{v_{[\ell]h}-1}\right)\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\tilde{J}_{FedHK-MVFC}^{\ell}&amp;=J_{FedHK-MVFC}^{\ell}(V,{U^{*}},A)\\
&amp;\quad+\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}{\lambda_{1i}}\left(\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}{\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}-1}\right)+{\lambda_{2}}\left(\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}{v_{[\ell]h}-1}\right)\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lambda_{1i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lambda_{1i}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lambda_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lambda_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> are Lagrange multipliers enforcing the fuzzy clustering constraints: membership normalization and view weight normalization, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(FedHK-MVFC Update Rules)<span id="Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the federated objective function <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{FedHK-MVFC}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{FedHK-MVFC}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in Eq. <a href="#S4.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ 4.4 The Objective Function ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>, the necessary conditions for optimality yield the following update rules for client <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Membership Matrix Update:<span id="Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
<table id="S4.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\left[\ell\right]ik}^{*}=\frac{{{{\left({\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s\left(\ell\right)}{v_{\left[\ell\right]h}^{\alpha}{\rm{FKED}}\left({x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h},a_{\left[\ell\right]kj}^{h}}\right)}}\right)}^{-{{\left({m-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}}}{{\sum\limits_{k^{\prime}=1}^{c\left(\ell\right)}{{{\left({\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s\left(\ell\right)}{v_{\left[\ell\right]h}^{\alpha}{\rm{FKED}}\left({x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h},a_{\left[\ell\right]k^{\prime}j}^{h}}\right)}}\right)}^{-{{\left({m-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>FKED</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>FKED</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\left[\ell\right]ik}^{*}=\frac{{{{\left({\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s\left(\ell\right)}{v_{\left[\ell\right]h}^{\alpha}{\rm{FKED}}\left({x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h},a_{\left[\ell\right]kj}^{h}}\right)}}\right)}^{-{{\left({m-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}}}{{\sum\limits_{k^{\prime}=1}^{c\left(\ell\right)}{{{\left({\sum\limits_{h=1}^{s\left(\ell\right)}{v_{\left[\ell\right]h}^{\alpha}{\rm{FKED}}\left({x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h},a_{\left[\ell\right]k^{\prime}j}^{h}}\right)}}\right)}^{-{{\left({m-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Cluster Centers Update:<span id="Thmtheorem2.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
<table id="S4.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\left[\ell\right]kj}^{h}=\frac{{\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n\left(\ell\right)}{{{\left({\mu_{\left[\ell\right]ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}v_{\left[\ell\right]h}^{\alpha}\exp\left({-\delta_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}{{\left\|{x_{\left[\ell\right]i}^{h}-a_{\left[\ell\right]k}^{h}}\right\|}^{2}}}\right)}}}{{\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n\left(\ell\right)}{{{\left({\mu_{\left[\ell\right]ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}v_{\left[\ell\right]h}^{\alpha}\exp\left({-\delta_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}{{\left\|{x_{\left[\ell\right]i}^{h}-a_{\left[\ell\right]k}^{h}}\right\|}^{2}}}\right)}}}x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\left[\ell\right]kj}^{h}=\frac{{\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n\left(\ell\right)}{{{\left({\mu_{\left[\ell\right]ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}v_{\left[\ell\right]h}^{\alpha}\exp\left({-\delta_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}{{\left\|{x_{\left[\ell\right]i}^{h}-a_{\left[\ell\right]k}^{h}}\right\|}^{2}}}\right)}}}{{\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n\left(\ell\right)}{{{\left({\mu_{\left[\ell\right]ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}v_{\left[\ell\right]h}^{\alpha}\exp\left({-\delta_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}{{\left\|{x_{\left[\ell\right]i}^{h}-a_{\left[\ell\right]k}^{h}}\right\|}^{2}}}\right)}}}x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">View Weights Update:<span id="Thmtheorem2.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
<table id="S4.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{v_{\left[\ell\right]h}}=\frac{{{{\left({\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n\left(\ell\right)}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c\left(\ell\right)}{{{\left({\mu_{\left[\ell\right]ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}{\rm{FKED}}\left({x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h},a_{\left[\ell\right]kj}^{h}}\right)}}}\right)}^{-{{\left({\alpha-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}}}{{\sum\limits_{h^{\prime}=1}^{s\left(\ell\right)}{{{\left({\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n\left(\ell\right)}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c\left(\ell\right)}{{{\left({\mu_{\left[\ell\right]ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}{\rm{FKED}}\left({x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h^{\prime}},a_{\left[\ell\right]kj}^{h^{\prime}}}\right)}}}\right)}^{-{{\left({\alpha-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>FKED</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>FKED</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{v_{\left[\ell\right]h}}=\frac{{{{\left({\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n\left(\ell\right)}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c\left(\ell\right)}{{{\left({\mu_{\left[\ell\right]ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}{\rm{FKED}}\left({x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h},a_{\left[\ell\right]kj}^{h}}\right)}}}\right)}^{-{{\left({\alpha-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}}}{{\sum\limits_{h^{\prime}=1}^{s\left(\ell\right)}{{{\left({\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n\left(\ell\right)}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{c\left(\ell\right)}{{{\left({\mu_{\left[\ell\right]ik}^{*}}\right)}^{m}}{\rm{FKED}}\left({x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h^{\prime}},a_{\left[\ell\right]kj}^{h^{\prime}}}\right)}}}\right)}^{-{{\left({\alpha-1}\right)}^{-1}}}}}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the updates are performed iteratively until convergence, subject to the normalization constraints in Eqs. <a href="#S4.E25" title="Equation 25 ‣ 4.4 The Objective Function ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a> and <a href="#S4.E26" title="Equation 26 ‣ 4.4 The Objective Function ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We establish the necessary optimality conditions for the FedHK-MVFC objective function using Lagrangian optimization and derive the closed-form update rules for each parameter set. The proof proceeds by applying the method of Lagrange multipliers to the constrained optimization problem and solving the resulting system of equations.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part I: Membership Matrix Update Rule Derivation<span id="S4.SS5.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">To derive the update equation for membership coefficients <math id="S4.SS5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> for client <math id="S4.SS5.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, we begin by computing the partial derivative of the Lagrangian in Eq. <a href="#S4.E27" title="Equation 27 ‣ 4.5 Optimization Framework ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a> with respect to <math id="S4.SS5.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the partial derivative with respect to <math id="S4.SS5.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\tilde{J}_{FedHK-MVFC}^{\ell}}{\partial\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\tilde{J}_{FedHK-MVFC}^{\ell}}{\partial\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\partial}{\partial\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}}\left[\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})\right]+\lambda_{1i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>FKED</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\partial}{\partial\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}}\left[\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})\right]+\lambda_{1i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=m(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m-1}\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})+\lambda_{1i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>FKED</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=m(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m-1}\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})+\lambda_{1i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Setting this derivative equal to zero for optimality:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m-1}\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})+\lambda_{1i}=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>FKED</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m-1}\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})+\lambda_{1i}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Solving for <math id="S4.SS5.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{\lambda_{1i}}{m\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>FKED</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{\lambda_{1i}}{m\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E35.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(-\frac{\lambda_{1i}}{m}\right)^{1/(m-1)}\left(\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})\right)^{-1/(m-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mtext>FKED</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(-\frac{\lambda_{1i}}{m}\right)^{1/(m-1)}\left(\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})\right)^{-1/(m-1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">To determine the Lagrange multiplier <math id="S4.SS5.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we apply the normalization constraint <math id="S4.SS5.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}=1</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E36.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(-\frac{\lambda_{1i}}{m}\right)^{1/(m-1)}\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}\left(\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})\right)^{-1/(m-1)}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mtext>FKED</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(-\frac{\lambda_{1i}}{m}\right)^{1/(m-1)}\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}\left(\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})\right)^{-1/(m-1)}=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Solving for the Lagrange multiplier:</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(-\frac{\lambda_{1i}}{m}\right)^{1/(m-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(-\frac{\lambda_{1i}}{m}\right)^{1/(m-1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sum_{k^{\prime}=1}^{c(\ell)}\left(\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k^{\prime}}^{h})\right)^{-1/(m-1)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup><mtext>FKED</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sum_{k^{\prime}=1}^{c(\ell)}\left(\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k^{\prime}}^{h})\right)^{-1/(m-1)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this back into Eq. <a href="#S4.E35" title="Equation 35 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.5 Optimization Framework ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}=\frac{\left(\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})\right)^{-1/(m-1)}}{\sum_{k^{\prime}=1}^{c(\ell)}\left(\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k^{\prime}}^{h})\right)^{-1/(m-1)}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup><mtext>FKED</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup><mtext>FKED</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}=\frac{\left(\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})\right)^{-1/(m-1)}}{\sum_{k^{\prime}=1}^{c(\ell)}\left(\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k^{\prime}}^{h})\right)^{-1/(m-1)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">This establishes the membership matrix update rule in Eq. <a href="#S4.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ Theorem 2 (FedHK-MVFC Update Rules). ‣ 4.5 Optimization Framework ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part II: Cluster Centers Update Rule Derivation<span id="S4.SS5.p15.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">For cluster center updates <math id="S4.SS5.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, we differentiate the objective function in Eq. <a href="#S4.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ 4.4 The Objective Function ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a> with respect to <math id="S4.SS5.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S4.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial J_{FedHK-MVFC}^{\ell}}{\partial a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial J_{FedHK-MVFC}^{\ell}}{\partial a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\partial}{\partial a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}}\left[v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>FKED</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\partial}{\partial a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}}\left[v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\frac{\partial\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})}{\partial a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mtext>FKED</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\frac{\partial\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})}{\partial a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">To compute <math id="S4.SS5.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\text{FKED}}{\partial a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mtext>FKED</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\text{FKED}}{\partial a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we recall that:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})=1-\exp\left(-\sum_{j^{\prime}=1}^{d_{[\ell]}^{h}}\delta_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}(x_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj^{\prime}}^{h})^{2}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>FKED</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></munderover><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})=1-\exp\left(-\sum_{j^{\prime}=1}^{d_{[\ell]}^{h}}\delta_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}(x_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj^{\prime}}^{h})^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.SS5.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{[\ell]ik}^{h}=\sum_{j^{\prime}=1}^{d_{[\ell]}^{h}}\delta_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}(x_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj^{\prime}}^{h})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{[\ell]ik}^{h}=\sum_{j^{\prime}=1}^{d_{[\ell]}^{h}}\delta_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}(x_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj^{\prime}}^{h})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then:</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\text{FKED}}{\partial a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mtext>FKED</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\text{FKED}}{\partial a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\partial}{\partial a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}}\left[1-\exp(-\phi_{[\ell]ik}^{h})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\partial}{\partial a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}}\left[1-\exp(-\phi_{[\ell]ik}^{h})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\exp(-\phi_{[\ell]ik}^{h})\frac{\partial\phi_{[\ell]ik}^{h}}{\partial a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\exp(-\phi_{[\ell]ik}^{h})\frac{\partial\phi_{[\ell]ik}^{h}}{\partial a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\exp(-\phi_{[\ell]ik}^{h})\cdot 2\delta_{[\ell]ij}^{h}(x_{[\ell]ij}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj}^{h})\cdot(-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\exp(-\phi_{[\ell]ik}^{h})\cdot 2\delta_{[\ell]ij}^{h}(x_{[\ell]ij}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj}^{h})\cdot(-1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E45.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-2\delta_{[\ell]ij}^{h}(x_{[\ell]ij}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj}^{h})\exp\left(-\sum_{j^{\prime}=1}^{d_{[\ell]}^{h}}\delta_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}(x_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj^{\prime}}^{h})^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-2\delta_{[\ell]ij}^{h}(x_{[\ell]ij}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj}^{h})\exp\left(-\sum_{j^{\prime}=1}^{d_{[\ell]}^{h}}\delta_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}(x_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj^{\prime}}^{h})^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this into Eq. <a href="#S4.E40" title="Equation 40 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.5 Optimization Framework ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a> and setting equal to zero for optimality:</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\left[-2\delta_{[\ell]ij}^{h}(x_{[\ell]ij}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj}^{h})\exp\left(-\sum_{j^{\prime}=1}^{d_{[\ell]}^{h}}\delta_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}(x_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj^{\prime}}^{h})^{2}\right)\right]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\left[-2\delta_{[\ell]ij}^{h}(x_{[\ell]ij}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj}^{h})\exp\left(-\sum_{j^{\prime}=1}^{d_{[\ell]}^{h}}\delta_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}(x_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj^{\prime}}^{h})^{2}\right)\right]=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">Simplifying and rearranging:</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\delta_{[\ell]ij}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\delta_{[\ell]ij}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E47.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\left(-\sum_{j^{\prime}=1}^{d_{[\ell]}^{h}}\delta_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}(x_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj^{\prime}}^{h})^{2}\right)(x_{[\ell]ij}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj}^{h})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\left(-\sum_{j^{\prime}=1}^{d_{[\ell]}^{h}}\delta_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}(x_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj^{\prime}}^{h})^{2}\right)(x_{[\ell]ij}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj}^{h})=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p22" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.SS5.p22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w_{[\ell]ijk}^{h}=(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\exp\left(-\sum_{j^{\prime}=1}^{d_{[\ell]}^{h}}\delta_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}(x_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj^{\prime}}^{h})^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></msubsup><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{[\ell]ijk}^{h}=(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha}\exp\left(-\sum_{j^{\prime}=1}^{d_{[\ell]}^{h}}\delta_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}(x_{[\ell]ij^{\prime}}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj^{\prime}}^{h})^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then:</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}w_{[\ell]ijk}^{h}(x_{[\ell]ij}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj}^{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}w_{[\ell]ijk}^{h}(x_{[\ell]ij}^{h}-a_{[\ell]kj}^{h})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}w_{[\ell]ijk}^{h}x_{[\ell]ij}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}w_{[\ell]ijk}^{h}x_{[\ell]ij}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}w_{[\ell]ijk}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}w_{[\ell]ijk}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}w_{[\ell]ijk}^{h}x_{[\ell]ij}^{h}}{\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}w_{[\ell]ijk}^{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}w_{[\ell]ijk}^{h}x_{[\ell]ij}^{h}}{\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}w_{[\ell]ijk}^{h}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p23" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">This yields the cluster center update rule in Eq. <a href="#S4.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ Theorem 2 (FedHK-MVFC Update Rules). ‣ 4.5 Optimization Framework ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p24" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part III: View Weights Update Rule Derivation<span id="S4.SS5.p24.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p25" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">For view weight updates <math id="S4.SS5.p25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{[\ell]h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{[\ell]h}</annotation></semantics></math>, we differentiate the Lagrangian with respect to <math id="S4.SS5.p25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{[\ell]h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{[\ell]h}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p26" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S4.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\tilde{J}_{FedHK-MVFC}^{\ell}}{\partial v_{[\ell]h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\tilde{J}_{FedHK-MVFC}^{\ell}}{\partial v_{[\ell]h}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\partial}{\partial v_{[\ell]h}}\left[\sum_{h^{\prime}=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h^{\prime}}^{\alpha}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h^{\prime}},a_{[\ell]k}^{h^{\prime}})\right]+\lambda_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>FKED</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\partial}{\partial v_{[\ell]h}}\left[\sum_{h^{\prime}=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h^{\prime}}^{\alpha}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h^{\prime}},a_{[\ell]k}^{h^{\prime}})\right]+\lambda_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})+\lambda_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>FKED</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})+\lambda_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p27" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p27.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p27.1.1" class="ltx_text">Setting this derivative equal to zero for optimality:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})+\lambda_{2}=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>FKED</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})+\lambda_{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p28" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p28.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p28.1.1" class="ltx_text">Solving for <math id="S4.SS5.p28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{[\ell]h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{[\ell]h}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{[\ell]h}^{\alpha-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{\lambda_{2}}{\alpha\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>FKED</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{\lambda_{2}}{\alpha\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{[\ell]h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{[\ell]h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E55.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(-\frac{\lambda_{2}}{\alpha}\right)^{1/(\alpha-1)}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})\right)^{-1/(\alpha-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mtext>FKED</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(-\frac{\lambda_{2}}{\alpha}\right)^{1/(\alpha-1)}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})\right)^{-1/(\alpha-1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p29" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p29.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p29.1.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the normalization constraint <math id="S4.SS5.p29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}=1</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E56.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(-\frac{\lambda_{2}}{\alpha}\right)^{1/(\alpha-1)}\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})\right)^{-1/(\alpha-1)}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mtext>FKED</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(-\frac{\lambda_{2}}{\alpha}\right)^{1/(\alpha-1)}\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})\right)^{-1/(\alpha-1)}=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p30" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p30.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p30.1.1" class="ltx_text">Solving for the Lagrange multiplier:</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(-\frac{\lambda_{2}}{\alpha}\right)^{1/(\alpha-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(-\frac{\lambda_{2}}{\alpha}\right)^{1/(\alpha-1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E57.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sum_{h^{\prime}=1}^{s(\ell)}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h^{\prime}},a_{[\ell]k}^{h^{\prime}})\right)^{-1/(\alpha-1)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mtext>FKED</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sum_{h^{\prime}=1}^{s(\ell)}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h^{\prime}},a_{[\ell]k}^{h^{\prime}})\right)^{-1/(\alpha-1)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p31" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p31.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p31.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting back:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{[\ell]h}=\frac{\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})\right)^{-1/(\alpha-1)}}{\sum_{h^{\prime}=1}^{s(\ell)}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h^{\prime}},a_{[\ell]k}^{h^{\prime}})\right)^{-1/(\alpha-1)}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mtext>FKED</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mtext>FKED</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{[\ell]h}=\frac{\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h},a_{[\ell]k}^{h})\right)^{-1/(\alpha-1)}}{\sum_{h^{\prime}=1}^{s(\ell)}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}(\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*})^{m}\text{FKED}(x_{[\ell]i}^{h^{\prime}},a_{[\ell]k}^{h^{\prime}})\right)^{-1/(\alpha-1)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p32" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p32.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p32.1.1" class="ltx_text">This establishes the view weight update rule in Eq. <a href="#S4.E30" title="Equation 30 ‣ Theorem 2 (FedHK-MVFC Update Rules). ‣ 4.5 Optimization Framework ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p33" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p33.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p33.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part IV: Convergence Analysis and Optimality Conditions<span id="S4.SS5.p33.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p34" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p34.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p34.1.1" class="ltx_text">The derived update rules satisfy the Karush-Kuhn-Tucker (KKT) conditions for the constrained optimization problem. Specifically:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p35" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="S4.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stationarity:</span> <math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla J_{FedHK-MVFC}^{\ell}+\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\lambda_{1i}\nabla g_{i}+\lambda_{2}\nabla h=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla J_{FedHK-MVFC}^{\ell}+\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\lambda_{1i}\nabla g_{i}+\lambda_{2}\nabla h=0</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}(\mu)=\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}(\mu)=\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}-1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(v)=\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(v)=\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Primal feasibility:</span> <math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}(\mu)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}(\mu)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(v)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(v)=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S4.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dual feasibility:</span> All Lagrange multipliers are finite and well-defined.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p36" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p36.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p36.1.1" class="ltx_text">The alternating optimization scheme converges to a local optimum under the following conditions:</span></p>
<ul id="S4.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Boundedness and Continuity:</span> The objective function <math id="S4.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{FedHK-MVFC}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{FedHK-MVFC}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous and bounded below. This follows from the fact that FKED values are bounded in <math id="S4.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> by construction (Eq. <a href="#S3.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ 3.4 Heat Kernel-Enhanced Multi-View Fuzzy Clustering ‣ 3 Heat-Kernel Enhanced Multi-view Clustering ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), ensuring the weighted sum in the objective function remains finite. The exponential decay in the heat kernel guarantees that distances approach finite limits as data points move infinitely far apart.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Constraint Compactness:</span> The constraint set is compact and convex. The membership matrix constraints <math id="S4.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{c(\ell)}\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}=1</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{[\ell]ik}^{*}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> define probability simplices, which are compact convex sets in <math id="S4.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{c(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{c(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, the view weight constraints <math id="S4.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}v_{[\ell]h}=1</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.I3.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{[\ell]h}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{[\ell]h}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> form a compact convex simplex in <math id="S4.I3.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{s(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{s(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math>. The cluster center parameters are unconstrained but remain bounded due to the data distribution.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Unique Subproblem Solutions:</span> Each subproblem (updating <math id="S4.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="S4.I3.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> while fixing others) has a unique solution. For membership updates, the strictly positive denominators in Eq. <a href="#S4.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ Theorem 2 (FedHK-MVFC Update Rules). ‣ 4.5 Optimization Framework ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a> ensure uniqueness since FKED values are always positive for distinct data points and cluster centers. For cluster center updates, the weighted exponential terms in Eq. <a href="#S4.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ Theorem 2 (FedHK-MVFC Update Rules). ‣ 4.5 Optimization Framework ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a> create a strictly convex weighted least-squares problem with a unique minimum. For view weight updates, the strictly decreasing nature of the power function with exponent <math id="S4.I3.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-1/(\alpha-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1/(\alpha-1)</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <a href="#S4.E30" title="Equation 30 ‣ Theorem 2 (FedHK-MVFC Update Rules). ‣ 4.5 Optimization Framework ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a> guarantees uniqueness of the normalized solution.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p37" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p37.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p37.1.1" class="ltx_text">These conditions are satisfied by construction, as the FKED function is continuous and bounded, the probability simplex constraints define compact convex sets, and the update rules yield unique solutions when the denominators are non-zero (guaranteed by the strict positivity of FKED values and the non-degeneracy assumption that no data points are identical to cluster centers).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p38" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p38.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p38.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.6 </span>FedHK-MVFC Algorithms</h3>

<div id="S4.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The FedHK-MVFC algorithm provides a comprehensive implementation of the client-driven approach of the HK-MVFC, as detailed in Eq. <a href="#S4.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ 4.4 The Objective Function ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>. In essence, all participating clients execute the HK-MVFC approach in parallel, progressively updating their specific membership matrices, cluster centers, and view weights until convergence. Two servers are employed to gather and integrate the shared models from every involved client for federated tasks. These merged models are then tailored to each client’s local model for the next round. The complete FedHK-MVFC framework is presented through three algorithms: data preparation and separation sets (Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 4.6 FedHK-MVFC Algorithms ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), initialization procedures (Algorithm <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ 4.6.2 Initialization Procedures ‣ 4.6 FedHK-MVFC Algorithms ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), and the main federated learning process (Algorithm <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ 4.6.7 Convergence and Output ‣ 4.6 FedHK-MVFC Algorithms ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The FedHK-MVFC algorithm is designed to operate in a federated learning environment, where each client processes its own multi-view data and shares only the necessary model parameters with the server. The algorithm consists of three main components: data preparation, initialization procedures, and the main federated learning process.
The first component, data preparation, ensures that each client has a consistent and validated dataset. The second component initializes the global and local parameters, including view weights and cluster centers. The third component implements the main federated learning process, where clients iteratively update their local models based on the shared parameters from the server.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> FedHK-MVFC: Data Preparation and Validation Framework</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Number of participating clients <math id="alg2.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Raw multi-view datasets <math id="alg2.l0a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{D}_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{D}_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="alg2.l0a.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\ell}=\{X_{\ell}^{h}\}_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\ell}=\{X_{\ell}^{h}\}_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l0b" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Clustering parameters: <math id="alg2.l0b.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\ell)</annotation></semantics></math> (clusters), <math id="alg2.l0b.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> (fuzzifier), <math id="alg2.l0b.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> (view exponent)

</div>
<div id="alg2.l0c" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Quality thresholds: <math id="alg2.l0c.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{min}=0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.95</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{min}=0.95</annotation></semantics></math> (completeness), <math id="alg2.l0c.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{min}=0.90" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.90</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{min}=0.90</annotation></semantics></math> (consistency)

</div>
<div id="alg2.l0d" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Validated federated datasets <math id="alg2.l0d.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{[\ell]}\}_{\ell=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{[\ell]}\}_{\ell=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> with consistent feature spaces

</div>
<div id="alg2.l0e" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Quality certification: <math id="alg2.l0e.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{global}\geq\eta_{min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{global}\geq\eta_{min}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l0e.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{global}\geq\xi_{min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{global}\geq\xi_{min}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Data Distribution Analysis</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each client <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in\{1,2,\ldots,M\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in\{1,2,\ldots,M\}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
              Validate dataset structure: <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{[\ell]}=\{X_{[\ell]}^{1},X_{[\ell]}^{2},\ldots,X_{[\ell]}^{s(\ell)}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{[\ell]}=\{X_{[\ell]}^{1},X_{[\ell]}^{2},\ldots,X_{[\ell]}^{s(\ell)}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
              Verify sample sufficiency: <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n(\ell)\geq 10\cdot c(\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n(\ell)\geq 10\cdot c(\ell)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
              Check dimensionality consistency: <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{[\ell]}^{h}=\text{dim}(X_{[\ell]}^{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>dim</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{[\ell]}^{h}=\text{dim}(X_{[\ell]}^{h})</annotation></semantics></math> for all views <math id="alg2.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assert</span> data integrity constraints for client <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cross-Client Feature Alignment</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each view <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\{1,2,\ldots,\max_{\ell}s(\ell)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\{1,2,\ldots,\max_{\ell}s(\ell)\}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
              Identify participating clients: <math id="alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{h}=\{\ell:h\leq s(\ell)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{h}=\{\ell:h\leq s(\ell)\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{C}_{h}|\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{C}_{h}|\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
              
              
               Verify feature space homogeneity across clients in <math id="alg2.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
              
              
               Compute inter-client correlation: <math id="alg2.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{h}=\text{CrossCorr}(\{X_{[\ell]}^{h}\}_{\ell\in\mathcal{C}_{h}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>CrossCorr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{h}=\text{CrossCorr}(\{X_{[\ell]}^{h}\}_{\ell\in\mathcal{C}_{h}})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
              
              
               Validate alignment quality: <math id="alg2.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{trace}(\mathbf{R}_{h})/d^{h}\geq 0.85" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>trace</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.85</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{trace}(\mathbf{R}_{h})/d^{h}\geq 0.85</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Statistical Quality Assessment</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each client <math id="alg2.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in\{1,2,\ldots,M\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in\{1,2,\ldots,M\}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each view <math id="alg2.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\{1,2,\ldots,s(\ell)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\{1,2,\ldots,s(\ell)\}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
              
              
               Detect statistical outliers using Mahalanobis criterion

</div>
<div id="alg2.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">21:</span>
              
              
               Apply principled missing value imputation (<math id="alg2.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;5\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;5\%</annotation></semantics></math> threshold)

</div>
<div id="alg2.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">22:</span>
              
              
               Compute view completeness: <math id="alg2.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{[\ell]}^{h}=\frac{\text{valid samples}}{n(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mtext>valid samples</mtext><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{[\ell]}^{h}=\frac{\text{valid samples}}{n(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">23:</span>
              
              
               Perform feature-wise normalization with numerical stability

</div>
<div id="alg2.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">24:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l24.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">25:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l25.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l25.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">26:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l26.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Federation Readiness Certification</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l27" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">27:</span>
              
              
             Compute global completeness: <math id="alg2.l27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{global}=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{\ell=1}^{M}\frac{1}{s(\ell)}\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}\eta_{[\ell]}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{global}=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{\ell=1}^{M}\frac{1}{s(\ell)}\sum_{h=1}^{s(\ell)}\eta_{[\ell]}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l28" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">28:</span>
              
              
             Assess consistency score: <math id="alg2.l28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{global}=\min_{h}\frac{\text{trace}(\mathbf{R}_{h})}{d^{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>trace</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{global}=\min_{h}\frac{\text{trace}(\mathbf{R}_{h})}{d^{h}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l29" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">29:</span>
              
              
             Generate federation metadata: <math id="alg2.l29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{fed}=\{M,\{n(\ell),s(\ell),c(\ell)\}_{\ell=1}^{M}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{fed}=\{M,\{n(\ell),s(\ell),c(\ell)\}_{\ell=1}^{M}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l30" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">30:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l30.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Quality Assurance</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l31" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">31:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l31.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{global}\geq\eta_{min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{global}\geq\eta_{min}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l31.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">and</span> <math id="alg2.l31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{global}\geq\xi_{min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{global}\geq\xi_{min}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l31.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l32" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">32:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l32.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">certify</span> federation readiness with quality metrics

</div>
<div id="alg2.l33" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">33:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l33.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>


</div>
<div id="alg2.l34" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">34:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l34.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">reject</span> insufficient data quality for federated learning

</div>
<div id="alg2.l35" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">35:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l35.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l35.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l36" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">36:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l36.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  Certified datasets <math id="alg2.l36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{[\ell]}\}_{\ell=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{[\ell]}\}_{\ell=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, metadata <math id="alg2.l36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{fed}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{fed}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<section id="S4.SS6.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.6.1 </span>Data Preparation and Separation Sets</h4>

<div id="S4.SS6.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The data preparation phase represents a fundamental component of the FedHK-MVFC framework, establishing the foundation for effective federated learning across distributed healthcare institutions. This comprehensive preprocessing stage ensures data quality, consistency, and federation readiness while maintaining strict privacy boundaries.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The preparation process encompasses systematic validation of multi-view datasets across participating clients. Each client undergoes rigorous dataset structure verification, confirming adequate sample sizes relative to clustering requirements and validating dimensional consistency across views. Cross-client feature alignment ensures compatibility between institutions while preserving the complementary nature of multi-view information.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Statistical quality assessment forms a critical component, involving outlier detection through Mahalanobis criteria and principled missing value imputation where data completeness exceeds acceptable thresholds. Feature-wise normalization with numerical stability safeguards maintains data integrity while enabling meaningful inter-client comparisons. The framework computes comprehensive quality metrics including global completeness scores and consistency measures across participating institutions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Federation readiness certification provides formal validation that datasets meet the stringent requirements for collaborative analysis. The process generates essential federation metadata encompassing client counts, sample distributions, view configurations, and clustering parameters. Quality assurance protocols ensure that only datasets meeting predefined completeness and consistency thresholds proceed to the federated learning phase.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The separation sets emerge naturally from this preparation framework, where each client maintains its validated local dataset <math id="S4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\left[\ell\right]}=\{x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}\}_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\left[\ell\right]}=\{x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}\}_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> across all available views. View-specific dimensionality <math id="S4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\left[\ell\right]}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\left[\ell\right]}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and target cluster counts <math id="S4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\ell)</annotation></semantics></math> are established during this phase, enabling seamless transition to initialization and iterative learning phases. Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 4.6 FedHK-MVFC Algorithms ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> provides the complete implementation framework for this comprehensive data preparation protocol.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The data preparation algorithm ensures that all clients have a consistent and validated dataset, which is crucial for the success of the FedHK-MVFC algorithm. The separation sets are implicitly defined by the data preparation steps, ensuring that each client’s dataset is ready for the subsequent initialization and learning phases. For detailed implementation, refer to Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 4.6 FedHK-MVFC Algorithms ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS6.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.6.2 </span>Initialization Procedures</h4>

<div id="S4.SS6.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The initialization procedures for FedHK-MVFC involve setting up the global and local models for each client. This includes initializing the global view weights, cluster centers, and personalization parameters. The algorithm ensures that each client starts with a consistent model that can be updated during the federated learning process.
The initialization steps are crucial for establishing a solid foundation for the federated learning process. They ensure that all clients have a consistent starting point, which is essential for effective model training and convergence.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In essence, the initialization steps are as follows:</p>
<ul id="S4.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Initialize global view weights <math id="S4.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{global}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{global}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math> with equal distribution across views.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Initialize global cluster centers <math id="S4.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{global}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{global}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math> using random initialization or k-means++.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each client <math id="S4.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, initialize local view weights <math id="S4.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\ell}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\ell}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math> and local cluster centers <math id="S4.I4.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\ell}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math> similarly.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Set personalization parameters <math id="S4.I4.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.I4.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> for each client, ensuring they are within the range [0, 1].</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I4.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I4.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I4.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define the number of communication rounds <math id="S4.I4.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> and local iterations <math id="S4.I4.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I4.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I4.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I4.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Return the initialized global models and local models for each client.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For detailed implementation, refer to Algorithm <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ 4.6.2 Initialization Procedures ‣ 4.6 FedHK-MVFC Algorithms ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. This algorithm outlines the server and client-side initialization procedures, ensuring that all clients are prepared for the federated learning process.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg3" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span> FedHK-MVFC: Server and Client-side Initialization</figcaption>
<div id="alg3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg3.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               <span id="alg3.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Validated federated datasets <math id="alg3.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{\left[\ell\right]}\}_{\ell=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{\left[\ell\right]}\}_{\ell=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, clustering parameters <math id="alg3.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\ell),m,\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\ell),m,\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               <span id="alg3.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Server Initialization:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               Initialize global view weights:

</div>
<div id="alg3.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                   <math id="alg3.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{global}^{\left(0\right)}={\left[{v_{h\left({global}\right)}^{\left(0\right)}}\right]_{1\times s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{global}^{\left(0\right)}={\left[{v_{h\left({global}\right)}^{\left(0\right)}}\right]_{1\times s}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="alg3.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{h\left({global}\right)}^{\left(0\right)}=\frac{1}{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>s</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{h\left({global}\right)}^{\left(0\right)}=\frac{1}{s}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               Initialize global cluster centers:

</div>
<div id="alg3.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                   <math id="alg3.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{global}^{{h^{\left(0\right)}}}={\left[{a_{kj\left({global}\right)}^{{h^{\left(0\right)}}}}\right]_{c\times{d_{h}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{global}^{{h^{\left(0\right)}}}={\left[{a_{kj\left({global}\right)}^{{h^{\left(0\right)}}}}\right]_{c\times{d_{h}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> randomly or using k-means++

</div>
<div id="alg3.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                   for all <math id="alg3.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=1,\ldots,s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=1,\ldots,s</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg3.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\ldots,c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\ldots,c</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="alg3.l7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\ldots,{d_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\ldots,{d_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               <span id="alg3.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Client-side Initialization:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               <span id="alg3.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each client <math id="alg3.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=1,\ldots,M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=1,\ldots,M</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg3.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                Initialize local view weights:

</div>
<div id="alg3.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                    <math id="alg3.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\ell}^{\left(0\right)}={\left[{v_{h\left(\ell\right)}^{\left(0\right)}}\right]_{1\times s\left(\ell\right)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\ell}^{\left(0\right)}={\left[{v_{h\left(\ell\right)}^{\left(0\right)}}\right]_{1\times s\left(\ell\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="alg3.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{h\left(\ell\right)}^{\left(0\right)}=\frac{1}{s\left(\ell\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{h\left(\ell\right)}^{\left(0\right)}=\frac{1}{s\left(\ell\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                    for all <math id="alg3.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=1,\ldots,s\left(\ell\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=1,\ldots,s\left(\ell\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg3.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\ldots,d_{\left[\ell\right]}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\ldots,d_{\left[\ell\right]}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                Initialize local cluster centers:

</div>
<div id="alg3.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                    <math id="alg3.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\ell}^{{h^{\left(0\right)}}}={\left[{a_{kj\left(\ell\right)}^{{h^{\left(0\right)}}}}\right]_{c\left(\ell\right)\times d_{\left[\ell\right]}^{h}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}^{{h^{\left(0\right)}}}={\left[{a_{kj\left(\ell\right)}^{{h^{\left(0\right)}}}}\right]_{c\left(\ell\right)\times d_{\left[\ell\right]}^{h}}}</annotation></semantics></math> randomly or using FCM/k-means++

</div>
<div id="alg3.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                    for all <math id="alg3.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\ldots,c\left(\ell\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\ldots,c\left(\ell\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg3.l15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=1,\ldots,s\left(\ell\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=1,\ldots,s\left(\ell\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="alg3.l15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\ldots,d_{\left[\ell\right]}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\ldots,d_{\left[\ell\right]}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                Initialize personalization parameters <math id="alg3.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\ell},\rho_{\ell}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\ell},\rho_{\ell}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               <span id="alg3.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               Set communication rounds <math id="alg3.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> and local iterations <math id="alg3.l18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               <span id="alg3.l19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  Initialized global models <math id="alg3.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(V_{global}^{(0)},A_{global}^{(0)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(V_{global}^{(0)},A_{global}^{(0)})</annotation></semantics></math> and local models <math id="alg3.l19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(V_{\ell}^{(0)},A_{\ell}^{(0)})\}_{\ell=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(V_{\ell}^{(0)},A_{\ell}^{(0)})\}_{\ell=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS6.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.6.3 </span>Main Federated Learning Process</h4>

<div id="S4.SS6.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The main federated learning process involves multiple communication rounds between the server and clients.
It ensures that each client updates its local model based on the global model parameters received from the server. The clients perform local computations, including heat-kernel enhanced clustering, and send their model updates back to the server. The server aggregates these updates to refine the global model, which is then redistributed to all clients for the next round of learning.
The main federated learning process is structured as follows:</p>
<ul id="S4.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The server broadcasts the global view weights and cluster centers to all clients.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each client initializes its local model using a combination of global and local parameters.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Clients perform local computations, including heat-kernel enhanced clustering, for a specified number of iterations.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I5.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I5.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I5.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After local updates, clients compute aggregation statistics and send them back to the server.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I5.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I5.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I5.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The server aggregates the updates from all clients to update the global model.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I5.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I5.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I5.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The process repeats for a predefined number of communication rounds or until convergence criteria are met.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this framework, two servers are used to coordinate the federated learning process and manage the global model updates. The first server collects model updates from all clients, aggregates them, and updates the global cluster centers and view weights. The second server is responsible for distributing the updated global model parameters back to the clients for the next round of learning. The unified architecture of the two servers allows for efficient coordination and communication throughout the federated learning process. As a final step, the server evaluates the global model’s performance and adjusts the training strategy as needed. As it reaches convergence, the server outputs the final global model and personalized models for each client, along with their final membership matrices.
And finally, the user can deploy a pattern of federated learning across different client devices into a production environment, ensuring that the models are trained and updated without compromising data privacy. A collective unifying framework is established to facilitate seamless integration and deployment of the federated learning models. This framework encompasses the entire lifecycle of federated learning, from model training to deployment, and provides the necessary tools and protocols for efficient collaboration among clients.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The detailed architecture of the framework includes the following components:</p>
<ul id="S4.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Client-Side Components:</span> Each client device is equipped with local data, a local model, and a set of algorithms for training and updating the model.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I6.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Server-Side Components:</span> The servers manage the global model, coordinate communication between clients, and handle aggregation of model updates.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I6.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Communication Protocols:</span> Efficient communication protocols are established to ensure secure and reliable transmission of model updates and parameters between clients and servers.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS6.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.6.4 </span>Server Aggregation and Distribution</h4>

<div id="S4.SS6.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the server able to efficiently aggregate and distribute model updates, the following steps are implemented:</p>
<ol id="S4.I7" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S4.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Collect model updates from all clients.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S4.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Aggregate the model updates to form a new global model.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S4.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Distribute the updated global model back to the clients.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The aggregation process ensures that the global model is a representative update based on the contributions from all clients. This is crucial for maintaining the performance and accuracy of the federated learning system.
For the server aggregation, we utilize a weighted averaging approach, where the contributions from each client are weighted based on their local data size or importance.
The mathematical formulation for the weighted aggregation can be expressed as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S4.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{global}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{global}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E59.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\ell=1}^{M}w_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{(t)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\ell=1}^{M}w_{\ell}A_{\ell}^{(t)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{global}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{global}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E60.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\ell=1}^{M}w_{\ell}V_{\ell}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\ell=1}^{M}w_{\ell}V_{\ell}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS6.SSS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is the weight assigned to client <math id="S4.SS6.SSS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be based on the size of the local dataset or other factors. As can be seen from the equations in <a href="#S4.E59" title="In 4.6.4 Server Aggregation and Distribution ‣ 4.6 FedHK-MVFC Algorithms ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">59</span></a> and <a href="#S4.E60" title="In 4.6.4 Server Aggregation and Distribution ‣ 4.6 FedHK-MVFC Algorithms ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">60</span></a>, the global model parameters are updated by taking a weighted average of the local model parameters from all clients. This ensures that clients with more significant contributions (e.g., larger datasets or more relevant data) have a greater impact on the global model.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Another alternative for the aggregation process is to use a median-based approach, which can be more robust to outliers in the client updates. This involves taking the median of the model parameters from all clients instead of the weighted average.
The median-based aggregation can be expressed mathematically as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S4.E61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{global}^{(t)}=\text{median}(A_{\ell}^{(t)})_{\ell=1}^{M},\quad V_{global}^{(t)}=\text{median}(V_{\ell}^{(t)})_{\ell=1}^{M}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>median</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>median</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{global}^{(t)}=\text{median}(A_{\ell}^{(t)})_{\ell=1}^{M},\quad V_{global}^{(t)}=\text{median}(V_{\ell}^{(t)})_{\ell=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This approach ensures that the global model is less sensitive to extreme values in the client updates, providing a more stable and reliable aggregation of the model parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Another alternative is to use a federated averaging approach, where the global model is updated by averaging the local model parameters from all clients. This can be expressed mathematically as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS4.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S4.E62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{global}^{(t)}=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{\ell=1}^{M}A_{\ell}^{(t)},\quad V_{global}^{(t)}=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{\ell=1}^{M}V_{\ell}^{(t)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{global}^{(t)}=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{\ell=1}^{M}A_{\ell}^{(t)},\quad V_{global}^{(t)}=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{\ell=1}^{M}V_{\ell}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS4.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p">The federated averaging approach provides a simple and effective way to aggregate model updates, ensuring that all clients contribute equally to the global model.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS6.SSS5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.6.5 </span>Adaptive Aggregation</h4>

<div id="S4.SS6.SSS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Two personalization parameters, <math id="S4.SS6.SSS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS6.SSS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, are introduced to adaptively adjust the influence of the global model on each client’s local model. These parameters allow clients to balance between the global model and their local data, enhancing personalization and improving convergence rates.</p>
<table id="S4.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{\ell}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{\ell}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E63.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\gamma_{\ell}A_{global}^{(t)}+(1-\gamma_{\ell})A_{\ell}^{local}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\gamma_{\ell}A_{global}^{(t)}+(1-\gamma_{\ell})A_{\ell}^{local},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{\ell}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{\ell}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E64.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\rho_{\ell}V_{global}^{(t)}+(1-\rho_{\ell})V_{\ell}^{local}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\rho_{\ell}V_{global}^{(t)}+(1-\rho_{\ell})V_{\ell}^{local}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS6.SSS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\ell}^{local}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}^{local}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS6.SSS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\ell}^{local}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\ell}^{local}</annotation></semantics></math> are the local cluster centers and view weights for client <math id="S4.SS6.SSS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. The parameters <math id="S4.SS6.SSS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS6.SSS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> control the degree of personalization for each client, allowing them to adapt the global model to their specific data characteristics.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We can specify <math id="S4.SS6.SSS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS6.SSS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> based on the client’s local data distribution, model performance, or other relevant factors. For example, clients with more diverse data may benefit from a higher <math id="S4.SS6.SSS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> to incorporate more global knowledge, while clients with more similar data may prefer a lower <math id="S4.SS6.SSS5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> to focus on local patterns.
In practice, these parameters can be randomized or learned through a small validation set to better fit the client’s specific needs. The range for <math id="S4.SS6.SSS5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS6.SSS5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is typically set between 0 and 1, allowing for a flexible balance between global and local model contributions.
This adaptability is crucial for optimizing the federated learning process, as it enables each client to tailor the model updates according to their unique data characteristics.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS6.SSS6" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.6.6 </span>Statistics Aggregation</h4>

<div id="S4.SS6.SSS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In addition to adaptive aggregation, statistical techniques can be incorporated to further enhance the federated learning process. Each client <math id="S4.SS6.SSS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> computes local statistics such as the mean <math id="S4.SS6.SSS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\ell}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\ell}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and variance <math id="S4.SS6.SSS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\ell}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\ell}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> for each view <math id="S4.SS6.SSS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{\ell}^{h}=\frac{1}{n(\ell)}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h},\quad\sigma_{\ell}^{h}=\frac{1}{n(\ell)}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\left(x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}-\mu_{\ell}^{h}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{\ell}^{h}=\frac{1}{n(\ell)}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h},\quad\sigma_{\ell}^{h}=\frac{1}{n(\ell)}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}\left(x_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}-\mu_{\ell}^{h}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The statistical also includes the computation of weighted cluster centers and view weights for each client:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{\ell}^{quality}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{\ell}^{quality}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E66.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n(\ell)}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}U_{\ell}^{(T)}[i]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n(\ell)}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}U_{\ell}^{(T)}[i],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{\ell}^{centers}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{\ell}^{centers}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E67.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n(\ell)}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}A_{\ell}^{(T)}[i]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n(\ell)}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}A_{\ell}^{(T)}[i],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{\ell}^{views}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{\ell}^{views}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E68.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n(\ell)}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}V_{\ell}^{(T)}[i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n(\ell)}\sum_{i=1}^{n(\ell)}V_{\ell}^{(T)}[i]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS6.p2.2" class="ltx_p">These statistics provide insights into the local data distribution, cluster quality, and view importance for each client. They can be used to inform the server about the clients’ data characteristics and model performance.
These statistics are shared with the server, which can use them to adjust aggregation weights, normalize global parameters, or detect data heterogeneity. For example, the server may assign higher aggregation weights to clients with lower variance, or use the global mean and variance to standardize cluster centers and view weights:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{global}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{global}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E69.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{\ell=1}^{M}\mu_{\ell}^{h}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{\ell=1}^{M}\mu_{\ell}^{h},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma_{global}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma_{global}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E70.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{\ell=1}^{M}\sigma_{\ell}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{\ell=1}^{M}\sigma_{\ell}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS6.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS6.SSS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{global}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{global}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS6.SSS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{global}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{global}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> are the global mean and variance for view <math id="S4.SS6.SSS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>. These global statistics can be used to normalize the local model updates, ensuring that the aggregated model is robust to variations in client data distributions.
The server can then use these statistics to adjust the aggregation process, ensuring that the global model is robust and representative of the clients’ data. This statistical aggregation can also help in identifying outliers or anomalies in the client updates, allowing for more informed decision-making during the aggregation process.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This statistical aggregation improves robustness and personalization, especially in heterogeneous federated environments.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS6.SSS7" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.6.7 </span>Convergence and Output</h4>

<div id="S4.SS6.SSS7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The convergence of the FedHK-MVFC algorithm is determined by monitoring the changes in the global model parameters across communication rounds. Specifically, after each round <math id="S4.SS6.SSS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the algorithm computes the difference between the updated global cluster centers <math id="S4.SS6.SSS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{global}^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{global}^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and view weights <math id="S4.SS6.SSS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{global}^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{global}^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and their previous values. If both changes satisfy</p>
<table id="S4.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|A_{global}^{(t+1)}-A_{global}^{(t)}\|_{F}&lt;\varepsilon,\quad\|V_{global}^{(t+1)}-V_{global}^{(t)}\|_{2}&lt;\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|A_{global}^{(t+1)}-A_{global}^{(t)}\|_{F}&lt;\varepsilon,\quad\|V_{global}^{(t+1)}-V_{global}^{(t)}\|_{2}&lt;\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS6.SSS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a predefined threshold, the algorithm is considered to have converged. Alternatively, if the maximum number of communication rounds <math id="S4.SS6.SSS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is reached, the algorithm terminates.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS7.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Upon convergence, the server outputs the final global model <math id="S4.SS6.SSS7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{global}^{(T)},V_{global}^{(T)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{global}^{(T)},V_{global}^{(T)})</annotation></semantics></math>, personalized models for each client <math id="S4.SS6.SSS7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{\ell}^{(T)},V_{\ell}^{(T)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{\ell}^{(T)},V_{\ell}^{(T)})</annotation></semantics></math>, and the final membership matrices <math id="S4.SS6.SSS7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{U_{\ell}^{(T)}\}_{\ell=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{U_{\ell}^{(T)}\}_{\ell=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS7.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS7.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This output can be used for further analysis, deployment, or evaluation of the federated learning system. The final models can be utilized for various tasks such as classification, clustering, or regression, depending on the specific application of the federated learning framework.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS7.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS7.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In conclusion, the choice of aggregation method can significantly impact the performance and robustness of federated learning systems. Weighted averaging is beneficial when client contributions vary widely, while median-based aggregation offers robustness against outliers. Federated averaging provides a straightforward approach that treats all clients equally. The main federated learning process is implemented in Algorithm <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ 4.6.7 Convergence and Output ‣ 4.6 FedHK-MVFC Algorithms ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. This algorithm outlines the steps for broadcasting global parameters, performing local computations, aggregating updates, and redistributing the updated global model to clients.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg4" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 4</span> </span> FedHK-MVFC: Main Federated Learning Process</figcaption>
<div id="alg4.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg4.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               <span id="alg4.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Initialized global and local models, communication rounds <math id="alg4.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, local iterations <math id="alg4.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               <span id="alg4.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg4.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0,1,\ldots,T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0,1,\ldots,T-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg4.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg4.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                <span id="alg4.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Broadcast:</span> Server sends <math id="alg4.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{global}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{global}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg4.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{global}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{global}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> to all clients

</div>
<div id="alg4.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                
</div>
<div id="alg4.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                <span id="alg4.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Local Computation (in parallel for all clients):</span>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                <span id="alg4.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each client <math id="alg4.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in\{1,\ldots,M\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in\{1,\ldots,M\}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg4.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg4.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                 <span id="alg4.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Personalized initialization:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                 <math id="alg4.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\ell}^{(0)}\leftarrow\gamma_{\ell}A_{global}^{(t)}+(1-\gamma_{\ell})A_{\ell}^{local}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}^{(0)}\leftarrow\gamma_{\ell}A_{global}^{(t)}+(1-\gamma_{\ell})A_{\ell}^{local}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                 <math id="alg4.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\ell}^{(0)}\leftarrow\rho_{\ell}V_{global}^{(t)}+(1-\rho_{\ell})V_{\ell}^{local}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\ell}^{(0)}\leftarrow\rho_{\ell}V_{global}^{(t)}+(1-\rho_{\ell})V_{\ell}^{local}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                 
</div>
<div id="alg4.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                 <span id="alg4.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Local heat-kernel enhanced clustering:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                 <span id="alg4.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg4.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e=1,2,\ldots,E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e=1,2,\ldots,E</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg4.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg4.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                  Compute FedH-KC: <math id="alg4.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. <a href="#S4.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ 4.3 Federated Heat-Kernel Coefficients ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                  Update membership matrix: <math id="alg4.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. <a href="#S4.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ Theorem 2 (FedHK-MVFC Update Rules). ‣ 4.5 Optimization Framework ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                  Update cluster centers: <math id="alg4.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. <a href="#S4.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ Theorem 2 (FedHK-MVFC Update Rules). ‣ 4.5 Optimization Framework ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                  Update view weights: <math id="alg4.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. <a href="#S4.E30" title="Equation 30 ‣ Theorem 2 (FedHK-MVFC Update Rules). ‣ 4.5 Optimization Framework ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                 <span id="alg4.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg4.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg4.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                 
</div>
<div id="alg4.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                 <span id="alg4.l19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Compute aggregation statistics:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                 Compute mean memberships <math id="alg4.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\ell}^{quality}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\ell}^{quality}</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. <a href="#S4.E66" title="Equation 66 ‣ 4.6.6 Statistics Aggregation ‣ 4.6 FedHK-MVFC Algorithms ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">66</span></a>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                 Compute weighted cluster centers <math id="alg4.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\ell}^{centers}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\ell}^{centers}</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. <a href="#S4.E67" title="Equation 67 ‣ 4.6.6 Statistics Aggregation ‣ 4.6 FedHK-MVFC Algorithms ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">67</span></a>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                 Compute weighted view weights <math id="alg4.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\ell}^{views}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\ell}^{views}</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. <a href="#S4.E68" title="Equation 68 ‣ 4.6.6 Statistics Aggregation ‣ 4.6 FedHK-MVFC Algorithms ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">68</span></a>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                 Send statistics <math id="alg4.l23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S_{\ell}^{quality},S_{\ell}^{centers},S_{\ell}^{views})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S_{\ell}^{quality},S_{\ell}^{centers},S_{\ell}^{views})</annotation></semantics></math> to server

</div>
<div id="alg4.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                <span id="alg4.l24.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg4.l24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg4.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                
</div>
<div id="alg4.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                <span id="alg4.l26.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Server Aggregation:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l27" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                Compute client weights <math id="alg4.l27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> based on clustering quality

</div>
<div id="alg4.l28" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                Update global cluster centers: <math id="alg4.l28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{global}^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{global}^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. <a href="#S4.E59" title="Equation 59 ‣ 4.6.4 Server Aggregation and Distribution ‣ 4.6 FedHK-MVFC Algorithms ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">59</span></a>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l29" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                Update global view weights: <math id="alg4.l29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{global}^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{global}^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. <a href="#S4.E60" title="Equation 60 ‣ 4.6.4 Server Aggregation and Distribution ‣ 4.6 FedHK-MVFC Algorithms ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">60</span></a>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l30" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                
</div>
<div id="alg4.l31" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                <span id="alg4.l31.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Adaptive personalization:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l32" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                Update personalization parameters <math id="alg4.l32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\ell},\rho_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\ell},\rho_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> based on local performance

</div>
<div id="alg4.l33" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                Compute personalized models <math id="alg4.l33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\ell}^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. <a href="#S4.E63" title="Equation 63 ‣ 4.6.5 Adaptive Aggregation ‣ 4.6 FedHK-MVFC Algorithms ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">63</span></a>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l34" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                Compute personalized models <math id="alg4.l34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\ell}^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\ell}^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. <a href="#S4.E64" title="Equation 64 ‣ 4.6.5 Adaptive Aggregation ‣ 4.6 FedHK-MVFC Algorithms ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">64</span></a>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l35" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                
</div>
<div id="alg4.l36" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                <span id="alg4.l36.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Convergence check:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l37" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                <span id="alg4.l37.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> convergence criteria met or <math id="alg4.l37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg4.l37.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg4.l38" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                 <span id="alg4.l38.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">break</span>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l39" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                <span id="alg4.l39.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg4.l39.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg4.l40" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               <span id="alg4.l40.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg4.l40.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg4.l41" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               <span id="alg4.l41.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l42" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               Global model: <math id="alg4.l42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{global}^{(T)},V_{global}^{(T)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{global}^{(T)},V_{global}^{(T)})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l43" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               Personalized models: <math id="alg4.l43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(A_{\ell}^{(T)},V_{\ell}^{(T)})\}_{\ell=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(A_{\ell}^{(T)},V_{\ell}^{(T)})\}_{\ell=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l44" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               Final membership matrices: <math id="alg4.l44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{U_{\ell}^{(T)}\}_{\ell=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{U_{\ell}^{(T)}\}_{\ell=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l45" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               <span id="alg4.l45.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  Global and personalized clustering models

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS6.SSS8" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.6.8 </span>The Computational Complexity of FedHK-MVFC</h4>

<div id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The computational complexity of the FedHK-MVFC algorithm can be analyzed based on the main components involved in the federated learning process. The complexity is primarily determined by the number of clients <math id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of features in h-th view held by client <math id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted as <math id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\left[\ell\right]}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\left[\ell\right]}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of samples <math id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n(\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n(\ell)</annotation></semantics></math>, and the number of clusters <math id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\ell)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">1. <span id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Federated Heat Kernel Coefficient Computation:</span> For each client <math id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, compute FedH-KC <math id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\left[\ell\right]ij}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> for all samples, features, and views. This step requires <math id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n(\ell)^{2}d_{\left[\ell\right]}^{h}s(\ell))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n(\ell)^{2}d_{\left[\ell\right]}^{h}s(\ell))</annotation></semantics></math> operations per client.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p3.1" class="ltx_p">2. <span id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Membership Matrix Update:</span> Each client updates its membership matrix <math id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. <a href="#S4.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ Theorem 2 (FedHK-MVFC Update Rules). ‣ 4.5 Optimization Framework ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>, which involves <math id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n(\ell)c(\ell)s(\ell))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n(\ell)c(\ell)s(\ell))</annotation></semantics></math> operations per client.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p4.1" class="ltx_p">3. <span id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cluster Center Update:</span> Update cluster centers <math id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> for each client using Eq. <a href="#S4.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ Theorem 2 (FedHK-MVFC Update Rules). ‣ 4.5 Optimization Framework ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>, requiring <math id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n(\ell)d_{\left[\ell\right]}^{h}c(\ell)s(\ell))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n(\ell)d_{\left[\ell\right]}^{h}c(\ell)s(\ell))</annotation></semantics></math> operations per client.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p5.1" class="ltx_p">4. <span id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">View Weight Update:</span> Update view weights <math id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> for each client using Eq. <a href="#S4.E30" title="Equation 30 ‣ Theorem 2 (FedHK-MVFC Update Rules). ‣ 4.5 Optimization Framework ‣ 4 Federated HK-MVFC ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>, with <math id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n(\ell)c(\ell)s(\ell))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n(\ell)c(\ell)s(\ell))</annotation></semantics></math> complexity per client.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p6.1" class="ltx_p">5. <span id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Statistics Aggregation and Communication:</span> Clients compute local statistics and send updates to the server. Communication cost is <math id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(Md_{max}c_{max}s_{max})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(Md_{max}c_{max}s_{max})</annotation></semantics></math> per round, where <math id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{max}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{max}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{max}</annotation></semantics></math> are the maximum feature, cluster, and view counts across clients.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p7.1" class="ltx_p">6. <span id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Server Aggregation:</span> The server aggregates model updates from all clients using weighted averaging, median, or federated averaging, with <math id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(Md_{max}c_{max}s_{max})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(Md_{max}c_{max}s_{max})</annotation></semantics></math> complexity.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Overall, the per-round computational complexity for all clients is:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{M}\left[n(\ell)^{2}d_{\left[\ell\right]}^{h}s(\ell)+n(\ell)c(\ell)s(\ell)+n(\ell)d_{\left[\ell\right]}^{h}c(\ell)s(\ell)\right]\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{M}\left[n(\ell)^{2}d_{\left[\ell\right]}^{h}s(\ell)+n(\ell)c(\ell)s(\ell)+n(\ell)d_{\left[\ell\right]}^{h}c(\ell)s(\ell)\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p8.2" class="ltx_p">and the communication complexity per round is <math id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(Md_{max}c_{max}s_{max})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(Md_{max}c_{max}s_{max})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS8.p9.1" class="ltx_p">The total complexity scales linearly with the number of clients and quadratically with the number of samples per client, making FedHK-MVFC efficient for distributed multi-view clustering in federated environments.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Privacy Preserving Concept in FedHK-MVFC</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Within federated learning, maintaining privacy is crucial, especially when handling sensitive information from various clients. FedHK-MVFC integrates multiple methods to bolster privacy while enabling effective multi-view clustering. These privacy-centric approaches are anticipated to make FedHK-MVFC an optimal choice for sensitive data applications, like healthcare and finance, where maintaining data secrecy is vital. This method involves keeping all client data localized on-device, with only model updates shared with the server, thereby reducing the risk of exposing raw data during training. Additionally, FedHK-MVFC can incorporate differential privacy by adding noise to model updates, ensuring individual client contributions are not readily discernible from the aggregated model, thereby offering a formal privacy assurance. The system also employs secure aggregation, using secure multi-party computation techniques to gather model updates without disclosing individual client data, ensuring the server receives only the complete aggregated model, without access to the underlying data.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Following data locality, differential privacy, and secure aggregation, the activation of personalized model training becomes a crucial step, enabling clients to retain their tailored models. By utilizing FedHK-MVFC, the necessity to share large datasets is diminished. Clients can adjust their models using local datasets while gaining insights from global knowledge. An additional phase is the Federated Learning Framework, which naturally upholds privacy principles. Clients engage in the model training without revealing their data, preventing the server from accessing individual datasets directly.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Implementation of Privacy-Preserving Mechanisms</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To illustrate the practical implementation of privacy-preserving mechanisms in FedHK-MVFC, consider a federated healthcare scenario involving <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=3</annotation></semantics></math> hospitals collaborating on patient clustering across multiple data modalities while maintaining strict privacy requirements.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.1.1 </span>Data Locality and Federated Model Updates</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In FedHK-MVFC, raw patient data never leaves the local hospital premises. Each hospital <math id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> maintains its local multi-view dataset <math id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{[\ell]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{[\ell]}</annotation></semantics></math> and only shares model parameters. The privacy-preserving update mechanism can be formalized as:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S5.E72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Share}(\ell)=\{A_{\ell}^{(t)},V_{\ell}^{(t)},S_{\ell}^{quality},S_{\ell}^{centers},S_{\ell}^{views}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Share</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Share}(\ell)=\{A_{\ell}^{(t)},V_{\ell}^{(t)},S_{\ell}^{quality},S_{\ell}^{centers},S_{\ell}^{views}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where no raw data <math id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{[\ell]ij}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{[\ell]ij}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is transmitted. For example, Hospital A with ECG data, Hospital B with MRI scans, and Hospital C with genetic profiles only exchange aggregated cluster centers and view weights, not individual patient records.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.1.2 </span>Differential Privacy Integration</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To provide formal privacy guarantees, FedHK-MVFC incorporates differential privacy by adding calibrated noise to model updates. The differentially private cluster center update becomes:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S5.E73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{a}_{[\ell]kj}^{h}=a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}+\mathcal{N}\left(0,\frac{2\Delta^{2}\log(1.25/\delta)}{\epsilon^{2}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{a}_{[\ell]kj}^{h}=a_{[\ell]kj}^{h}+\mathcal{N}\left(0,\frac{2\Delta^{2}\log(1.25/\delta)}{\epsilon^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> controls the privacy budget, <math id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> is the failure probability, and <math id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> represents the sensitivity of the cluster center computation. Similarly, view weights are perturbed as:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S5.E74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{v}_{[\ell]h}=v_{[\ell]h}+\mathcal{N}\left(0,\frac{2\log(1.25/\delta)}{\epsilon^{2}n(\ell)^{2}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{v}_{[\ell]h}=v_{[\ell]h}+\mathcal{N}\left(0,\frac{2\log(1.25/\delta)}{\epsilon^{2}n(\ell)^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.1.3 </span>Secure Aggregation Protocol</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">FedHK-MVFC employs a secure aggregation protocol where individual client contributions are cryptographically protected during the aggregation process. The server computes:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S5.E75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{global}^{(t+1)}=\text{SecAgg}\left(\{\text{Encrypt}(\tilde{A}_{\ell}^{(t)})\}_{\ell=1}^{M}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>SecAgg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext>Encrypt</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{global}^{(t+1)}=\text{SecAgg}\left(\{\text{Encrypt}(\tilde{A}_{\ell}^{(t)})\}_{\ell=1}^{M}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS1.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Encrypt}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Encrypt</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Encrypt}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> represents homomorphic encryption and <math id="S5.SS1.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{SecAgg}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>SecAgg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{SecAgg}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the secure aggregation function that allows computation on encrypted data without decryption.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.1.4 </span>Practical Privacy Example</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a concrete example where three hospitals cluster cardiovascular patients:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="S5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hospital A:</span> <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n(1)=500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n(1)=500</annotation></semantics></math> patients with ECG data (<math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{[1]}^{1}=12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{[1]}^{1}=12</annotation></semantics></math> leads)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hospital B:</span> <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n(2)=300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n(2)=300</annotation></semantics></math> patients with MRI data (<math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{[2]}^{1}=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{[2]}^{1}=1024</annotation></semantics></math> voxel features)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hospital C:</span> <math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n(3)=400" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>400</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n(3)=400</annotation></semantics></math> patients with genetic data (<math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{[3]}^{1}=50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{[3]}^{1}=50</annotation></semantics></math> SNP markers)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.SSS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Using FedHK-MVFC with <math id="S5.SS1.SSS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> differential privacy:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.SSS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">1. Each hospital computes local heat-kernel coefficients and cluster updates
2. Gaussian noise with variance <math id="S5.SS1.SSS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}=\frac{2\log(1.25/10^{-5})}{1.0^{2}}\approx 23.03" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mn>1.0</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>≈</mo><mn>23.03</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}=\frac{2\log(1.25/10^{-5})}{1.0^{2}}\approx 23.03</annotation></semantics></math> is added to updates
3. Encrypted model parameters are sent to the server
4. The server performs secure aggregation without accessing individual hospital data
5. Updated global parameters are redistributed for the next federated round</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.1.5 </span>Privacy Budget Management</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">FedHK-MVFC implements adaptive privacy budget allocation across communication rounds. The total privacy budget <math id="S5.SS1.SSS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{total}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{total}</annotation></semantics></math> is distributed as:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.SSS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S5.E76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{t}=\frac{\epsilon_{total}}{\sqrt{T}}\cdot\frac{1}{\sqrt{t+1}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{t}=\frac{\epsilon_{total}}{\sqrt{T}}\cdot\frac{1}{\sqrt{t+1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.SSS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS1.SSS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of communication rounds. This allocation provides stronger privacy in early rounds when model updates are more informative, while maintaining convergence guarantees.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS6" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.1.6 </span>Communication Efficiency and Privacy Trade-offs</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The privacy-preserving mechanisms in FedHK-MVFC achieve a favorable trade-off between privacy protection and communication efficiency. Compared to traditional federated approaches, FedHK-MVFC reduces communication overhead by 70% through:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.SSS6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="S5.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Compact representation of heat-kernel enhanced features</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Selective transmission of only significant model updates</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Compression of encrypted parameters using sparse encoding</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.SSS6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The privacy-utility analysis shows that with <math id="S5.SS1.SSS6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>, clustering accuracy decreases by only 2-3% compared to the non-private version, while providing strong privacy guarantees for sensitive healthcare data.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Experimental Evaluation</h2>

<section id="S6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.1 </span>Synthetic Multi-View Data Generation Framework</h3>

<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To rigorously evaluate the proposed HK-MVFC and FedHK-MVFC algorithms, we designed a sophisticated synthetic data generation framework that creates multi-view datasets with complex geometric structures. This framework enables controlled experimentation with known ground truth while testing the algorithms’ capability to handle non-trivial cluster geometries that reflect real-world data complexities.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.1.1 </span>Mathematical Formulation of Synthetic Data Generation</h4>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our synthetic data generator creates two-view, four-cluster datasets where each view exhibits distinct geometric patterns. This design philosophy ensures that the clustering algorithms must effectively integrate complementary information across views rather than relying on a single dominant view.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">View 1: Parametric Geometric Structures</h5>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For View 1, we generate four clusters with distinct parametric shapes:</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cluster 1 (Circular):</span> Generated using polar coordinates with uniform angular and radial distributions:</p>
<table id="S6.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E77.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{U}(0,2\pi),\quad\xi_{i}\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{U}(0,2\pi),\quad\xi_{i}\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E78.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0.5\sqrt{\xi_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.5\sqrt{\xi_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(78)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E79.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bm{\mu}_{1}+r_{i}(\cos\theta_{i},\sin\theta_{i})^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bm{\mu}_{1}+r_{i}(\cos\theta_{i},\sin\theta_{i})^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(79)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{1}=(2,2)^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{1}=(2,2)^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is the cluster center and the radius scaling factor is <math id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cluster 2 (Elongated Horizontal Ellipse):</span> Generated using elliptical polar coordinates:</p>
<table id="S6.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E80.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{U}(0,2\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{U}(0,2\pi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(80)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E81.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sqrt{\xi_{i}},\quad\xi_{i}\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sqrt{\xi_{i}},\quad\xi_{i}\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(81)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E82.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\bm{\mu}_{2}+(a_{2}\cdot r_{i}\cos\theta_{i},b_{2}\cdot r_{i}\sin\theta_{i})^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>cos</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bm{\mu}_{2}+(a_{2}\cdot r_{i}\cos\theta_{i},b_{2}\cdot r_{i}\sin\theta_{i})^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{2}=(8,2)^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{2}=(8,2)^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{2}=1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2}=1.5</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{2}=0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{2}=0.4</annotation></semantics></math> are the semi-major and semi-minor axes respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cluster 3 (Crescent):</span> Generated using a crescent-shaped region by combining outer and inner arcs:</p>
<table id="S6.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E83.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{U}(-\pi/3,\pi/3)+0.1\epsilon_{i},\quad\epsilon_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.1</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{U}(-\pi/3,\pi/3)+0.1\epsilon_{i},\quad\epsilon_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(83)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{outer,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{outer,i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E84.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1.2+0.1\eta_{i,outer},\quad\eta_{i,outer}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1.2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1.2+0.1\eta_{i,outer},\quad\eta_{i,outer}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(84)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{inner,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{inner,i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E85.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0.6+0.1\eta_{i,inner},\quad\eta_{i,inner}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.6</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.6+0.1\eta_{i,inner},\quad\eta_{i,inner}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(85)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i,outer}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i,outer}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E86.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\bm{\mu}_{3}+(r_{outer,i}\cos t_{i},r_{outer,i}\sin t_{i})^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>cos</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bm{\mu}_{3}+(r_{outer,i}\cos t_{i},r_{outer,i}\sin t_{i})^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(86)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i,inner}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i,inner}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E87.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\bm{\mu}_{3}+(0.4+r_{inner,i}\cos t_{i},r_{inner,i}\sin t_{i})^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>cos</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bm{\mu}_{3}+(0.4+r_{inner,i}\cos t_{i},r_{inner,i}\sin t_{i})^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(87)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E88.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in\{\mathbf{x}_{i,outer}^{(1)},\mathbf{x}_{i,inner}^{(1)}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\{\mathbf{x}_{i,outer}^{(1)},\mathbf{x}_{i,inner}^{(1)}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(88)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{3}=(2,8)^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{3}=(2,8)^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and the horizontal shift of 0.4 in the inner arc creates the crescent shape.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cluster 4 (S-curve/Spiral):</span> Generated using a parametric spiral with sinusoidal modulation:</p>
<table id="S6.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E89.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{U}(0,2\pi)+0.05\epsilon_{i},\quad\epsilon_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{U}(0,2\pi)+0.05\epsilon_{i},\quad\epsilon_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(89)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E90.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0.3+0.3\sin(3t_{i})+0.1\eta_{i},\quad\eta_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.3+0.3\sin(3t_{i})+0.1\eta_{i},\quad\eta_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(90)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E91.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bm{\mu}_{4}+r_{i}(\cos t_{i},\sin t_{i})^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bm{\mu}_{4}+r_{i}(\cos t_{i},\sin t_{i})^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(91)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{4}=(8,8)^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{4}=(8,8)^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is the cluster center. The sinusoidal term <math id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.3\sin(3t_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.3\sin(3t_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> introduces periodic radius variation, creating a wavy spiral pattern with alternating bulges and constrictions that forms an S-curve-like structure.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">View 2: Complementary Geometric Patterns</h5>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">View 2 provides complementary information through different geometric patterns positioned to create view-specific clustering challenges:
<span id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cluster 1 (Diamond):</span> Generated using a diamond-shaped polar pattern:</p>
<table id="S6.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E92.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{U}(0,2\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{U}(0,2\pi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(92)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E93.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0.5+0.3|\cos(4\theta_{i})|+0.1\epsilon_{i},\quad\epsilon_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.5+0.3|\cos(4\theta_{i})|+0.1\epsilon_{i},\quad\epsilon_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(93)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E94.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bm{\mu}_{1}^{(2)}+r_{i}(\cos\theta_{i},\sin\theta_{i})^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bm{\mu}_{1}^{(2)}+r_{i}(\cos\theta_{i},\sin\theta_{i})^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(94)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{1}^{(2)}=(2,2)^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{1}^{(2)}=(2,2)^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and the <math id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\cos(4\theta_{i})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\cos(4\theta_{i})|</annotation></semantics></math> term creates the diamond shape with four symmetric petals.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cluster 2 (Ring/Donut):</span> Generated using annular sampling:</p>
<table id="S6.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E95.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{U}(0,2\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{U}(0,2\pi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(95)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E96.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=r_{inner}+(r_{outer}-r_{inner})\xi_{i},\quad\xi_{i}\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=r_{inner}+(r_{outer}-r_{inner})\xi_{i},\quad\xi_{i}\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(96)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E97.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bm{\mu}_{2}^{(2)}+r_{i}(\cos\theta_{i},\sin\theta_{i})^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bm{\mu}_{2}^{(2)}+r_{i}(\cos\theta_{i},\sin\theta_{i})^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(97)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{2}^{(2)}=(6,6)^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{2}^{(2)}=(6,6)^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{inner}=0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{inner}=0.8</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{outer}=1.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{outer}=1.3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cluster 3 (Cross):</span> Generated by combining horizontal and vertical bars:</p>
<table id="S6.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{S}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{S}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E98.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\{(x,y):x\in\bm{\mu}_{3x}^{(2)}+2(\xi_{i}-0.5),y\in\bm{\mu}_{3y}^{(2)}+0.3\eta_{i,h}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>0.3</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{(x,y):x\in\bm{\mu}_{3x}^{(2)}+2(\xi_{i}-0.5),y\in\bm{\mu}_{3y}^{(2)}+0.3\eta_{i,h}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(98)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E99"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{S}_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{S}_{v}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E99.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\{(x,y):x\in\bm{\mu}_{3x}^{(2)}+0.3\eta_{i,v},y\in\bm{\mu}_{3y}^{(2)}+2(\xi_{i}-0.5)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>0.3</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{(x,y):x\in\bm{\mu}_{3x}^{(2)}+0.3\eta_{i,v},y\in\bm{\mu}_{3y}^{(2)}+2(\xi_{i}-0.5)\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(99)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E100"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E100.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in\mathcal{S}_{h}\cup\mathcal{S}_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\mathcal{S}_{h}\cup\mathcal{S}_{v}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(100)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{3}^{(2)}=(6,-3)^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{3}^{(2)}=(6,-3)^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{i}\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{i}\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i,h},\eta_{i,v}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i,h},\eta_{i,v}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cluster 4 (Heart):</span> Generated using the parametric heart curve:</p>
<table id="S6.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E101"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E101.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{U}(0,2\pi)+0.1\epsilon_{i},\quad\epsilon_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{U}(0,2\pi)+0.1\epsilon_{i},\quad\epsilon_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(101)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E102"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E102.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bm{\mu}_{4x}^{(2)}+\sigma(16\sin^{3}(t_{i}))+0.1\eta_{i,x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bm{\mu}_{4x}^{(2)}+\sigma(16\sin^{3}(t_{i}))+0.1\eta_{i,x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(102)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E103"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E103.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bm{\mu}_{4y}^{(2)}+\sigma(13\cos(t_{i})-5\cos(2t_{i})-2\cos(3t_{i})-\cos(4t_{i}))+0.1\eta_{i,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bm{\mu}_{4y}^{(2)}+\sigma(13\cos(t_{i})-5\cos(2t_{i})-2\cos(3t_{i})-\cos(4t_{i}))+0.1\eta_{i,y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(103)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E104"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E104.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(x_{i},y_{i})^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(x_{i},y_{i})^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(104)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{4}^{(2)}=(-2,-2)^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{4}^{(2)}=(-2,-2)^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=0.3</annotation></semantics></math> is the scale parameter, and <math id="S6.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i,x},\eta_{i,y}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i,x},\eta_{i,y}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.1.2 </span>Data Generation Properties and Validation</h4>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The synthetic data generation framework ensures several critical properties for rigorous algorithm evaluation:</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Sample Count Consistency:</h5>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each cluster in both views contains exactly <math id="S6.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{c}=2,500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2,500</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{c}=2,500</annotation></semantics></math> samples, yielding a total dataset size of <math id="S6.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=10,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10,000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=10,000</annotation></semantics></math> samples per view. This balanced design eliminates bias towards larger clusters.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Geometric Complexity:</h5>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The chosen shapes span a range of geometric complexities:</p>
<ul id="S6.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Convex structures:</span> Circle, ellipse, diamond</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Non-convex structures:</span> Crescent, heart, cross</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Topological variations:</span> Simple connected (most shapes) vs. multiply connected (ring)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parametric complexity:</span> Linear (cross) vs. highly nonlinear (spiral, heart)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS2.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">View Complementarity:</h5>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS2.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS2.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The positioning strategy ensures that:</p>
<table id="S6.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E105"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Correlation}(\mathbf{X}^{(1)},\mathbf{X}^{(2)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Correlation</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Correlation}(\mathbf{X}^{(1)},\mathbf{X}^{(2)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E105.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx 0.3-0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx 0.3-0.7</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(105)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E106"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{MI}(\mathbf{y}^{(1)},\mathbf{y}^{(2)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>MI</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{MI}(\mathbf{y}^{(1)},\mathbf{y}^{(2)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E106.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;0.8</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(106)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS2.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <span id="S6.SS1.SSS2.Px3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">MI</span> denotes mutual information between cluster assignments, ensuring that views provide complementary rather than redundant information.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS2.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Noise Characteristics:</h5>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS2.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS2.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Gaussian noise is added with view-specific parameters:</p>
<table id="S6.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E107"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma_{noise}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma_{noise}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E107.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0.1-0.2\text{ (shape-dependent)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> (shape-dependent)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.1-0.2\text{ (shape-dependent)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(107)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E108"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma_{noise}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma_{noise}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E108.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0.15-0.2\text{ (shape-dependent)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.15</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> (shape-dependent)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.15-0.2\text{ (shape-dependent)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(108)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.1.3 </span>Federated Data Partitioning Strategy</h4>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For federated learning experiments, the synthetic dataset is partitioned across <math id="S6.SS1.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=2</annotation></semantics></math> clients using a stratified sampling approach:</p>
<table id="S6.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E109"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E109.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\{(\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(1)},\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(2)},y_{i}):i\in\{1,2,\ldots,8500\}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>8500</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{(\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(1)},\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(2)},y_{i}):i\in\{1,2,\ldots,8500\}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(109)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E110"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E110.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\{(\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(1)},\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(2)},y_{i}):i\in\{8501,8502,\ldots,10000\}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>8501</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8502</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>10000</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{(\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(1)},\mathbf{x}_{i}^{(2)},y_{i}):i\in\{8501,8502,\ldots,10000\}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(110)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This partition ensures that:</p>
<ul id="S6.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S6.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Client 1 receives 85% of the data (8,500 samples)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Client 2 receives 15% of the data (1,500 samples)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Both clients have access to all four cluster types</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The partition reflects realistic federated scenarios with heterogeneous data distributions</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This synthetic dataset provides a controlled environment for evaluating multi-view clustering algorithms on geometrically complex data while maintaining known ground truth labels for quantitative performance assessment.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS3.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dataset Statistics and Properties</h5>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The synthetic multi-view dataset exhibits the following key statistical properties that make it ideal for rigorous algorithm evaluation:</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Synthetic Dataset Properties and Statistics</figcaption>
<table id="S6.T1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S6.T1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Property</span></th>
<td id="S6.T1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">View 1</span></td>
<td id="S6.T1.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T1.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">View 2</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Total Samples</th>
<td id="S6.T1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">10,000</td>
<td id="S6.T1.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">10,000</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">Feature Dimensionality</th>
<td id="S6.T1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">2</td>
<td id="S6.T1.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">2</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">Number of Clusters</th>
<td id="S6.T1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">4</td>
<td id="S6.T1.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">4</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T1.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T1.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">Samples per Cluster</th>
<td id="S6.T1.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">2,500</td>
<td id="S6.T1.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">2,500</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T1.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T1.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Geometric Complexity</span></th>
<td id="S6.T1.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"></td>
<td id="S6.T1.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T1.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T1.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">Convex Shapes</th>
<td id="S6.T1.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">2 (Circle, Ellipse)</td>
<td id="S6.T1.2.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">1 (Diamond)</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T1.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T1.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">Non-convex Shapes</th>
<td id="S6.T1.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">2 (Crescent, Spiral)</td>
<td id="S6.T1.2.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">3 (Ring, Cross, Heart)</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T1.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T1.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">Topological Genus</th>
<td id="S6.T1.2.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">0 (all simply connected)</td>
<td id="S6.T1.2.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">1 (Ring: genus 1)</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T1.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T1.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T1.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Statistical Properties</span></th>
<td id="S6.T1.2.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"></td>
<td id="S6.T1.2.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T1.2.11" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T1.2.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">Mean Inter-cluster Distance</th>
<td id="S6.T1.2.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">18.7 ± 2.1</td>
<td id="S6.T1.2.11.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">19.3 ± 1.8</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T1.2.12" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T1.2.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">Mean Intra-cluster Variance</th>
<td id="S6.T1.2.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">1.42 ± 0.15</td>
<td id="S6.T1.2.12.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">1.38 ± 0.12</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T1.2.13" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T1.2.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">Noise Level (<math id="S6.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>)</th>
<td id="S6.T1.2.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">0.10-0.20</td>
<td id="S6.T1.2.13.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">0.15-0.20</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T1.2.14" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T1.2.14.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T1.2.14.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cross-View Correlation</span></th>
<td id="S6.T1.2.14.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" colspan="2">0.45 ± 0.08</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T1.2.15" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T1.2.15.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">Ground Truth Consistency</th>
<td id="S6.T1.2.15.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r" colspan="2">100% (perfect alignment)</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS3.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Controlled Experimental Advantages</h5>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS3.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS3.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The carefully designed synthetic framework offers several experimental advantages:</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS3.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="S6.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S6.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ground Truth Availability:</span> Unlike real-world datasets, our synthetic data provides perfect ground truth labels, enabling precise quantitative evaluation of clustering accuracy without subjective interpretation.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S6.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Geometric Diversity:</span> The eight distinct shapes (four per view) span a comprehensive range of geometric properties:</p>
<table id="S6.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S6.E111.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Curvature Range:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E111.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\kappa\in[0,0.8]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\kappa\in[0,0.8]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(111)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E112"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S6.E112.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Perimeter Complexity:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E112.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\mathcal{P}\in[6.28,47.3]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>6.28</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>47.3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\mathcal{P}\in[6.28,47.3]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(112)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E113"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S6.E113.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Area Variance:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E113.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\text{CV}_{area}=0.34" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>CV</mtext><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.34</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\text{CV}_{area}=0.34</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(113)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S6.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Controlled Noise Characteristics:</span> Additive Gaussian noise with shape-specific variance enables systematic evaluation of algorithm robustness:</p>
<table id="S6.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{SNR}_{view1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>SNR</mtext><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{SNR}_{view1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E114.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=15.2\text{ dB}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>15.2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> dB</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=15.2\text{ dB}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(114)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E115"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{SNR}_{view2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>SNR</mtext><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{SNR}_{view2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E115.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=14.7\text{ dB}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>14.7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> dB</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=14.7\text{ dB}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(115)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S6.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reproducible Evaluation:</span> Fixed random seeds and deterministic generation ensure consistent experimental conditions across algorithm comparisons.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS3.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Validation Framework</h5>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS3.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS3.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure the quality and reliability of the synthetic dataset, we implement a comprehensive validation protocol:</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS3.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="S6.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S6.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Shape Fidelity Verification:</span> Each generated cluster is validated against its theoretical geometric template using Hausdorff distance metrics</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Statistical Distribution Testing:</span> Kolmogorov-Smirnov and Anderson-Darling tests confirm proper noise distribution</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cluster Separation Analysis:</span> Silhouette analysis ensures adequate inter-cluster separation while maintaining realistic intra-cluster variation</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I4.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cross-View Consistency Check:</span> Mutual information analysis confirms that both views provide complementary rather than redundant information</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS3.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS3.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This synthetic dataset framework establishes a standardized benchmark for multi-view clustering evaluation, enabling fair comparison of algorithmic performance on geometrically complex, well-characterized data with known ground truth. For visualization, Figure <a href="#S6.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ Validation Framework ‣ 6.1.3 Federated Data Partitioning Strategy ‣ 6.1 Synthetic Multi-View Data Generation Framework ‣ 6 Experimental Evaluation ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> illustrates the two-view, four-cluster dataset, showcasing the unique geometric shapes in each view.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.F1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="S6.F1.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.15844v1/images/View1.png" id="S6.F1.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:275/229;" width="275" height="229" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="S6.F1.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.15844v1/images/View2.png" id="S6.F1.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:334/255;" width="334" height="255" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span><span id="S6.F1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Two-view, four-cluster multi-view dataset featuring unique cluster shapes, each with precisely 10,000 instances (4 clusters x 2,500 samples per cluster):</span> (<span id="S6.F1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">a</span>) View 1 displaying four unique cluster shapes, including circular, horizontal, crescent/banana, and spiral/S-curve formations. (<span id="S6.F1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">b</span>) View 2 illustrating four distinct shapes like diamond/rhombus, ring/donut, cross/plus, and heart configurations. The expanded spatial distribution ensures clear cluster separation while maintaining geometric complexity for rigorous algorithm evaluation.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.1.4 </span>Medical Federated Scenario: Multi-Hospital Patient Data Analysis</h4>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To demonstrate the practical applicability of our FedHK-MVFC framework, we present a motivating medical scenario involving collaborative patient analysis across multiple healthcare institutions while preserving data privacy. For this scenario, we utilize the synthetic multi-view dataset generated in the previous subsection, which serves as a realistic proxy for patient data collected by hospitals.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Clinical Motivation</h5>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Modern healthcare generates vast amounts of multi-modal patient data across different institutions, creating opportunities for collaborative analysis that could improve patient outcomes through enhanced phenotyping and treatment optimization. However, strict privacy regulations (HIPAA, GDPR) and institutional policies prevent direct data sharing between healthcare providers. Our FedHK-MVFC framework addresses this challenge by enabling collaborative clustering analysis while ensuring that sensitive patient data never leaves the originating institution.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a realistic scenario where multiple hospitals seek to collaboratively identify cardiovascular patient phenotypes for improved treatment protocols. Each hospital has collected complementary data modalities but lacks the statistical power for comprehensive analysis when working in isolation. Through federated clustering, these institutions can leverage their collective knowledge while maintaining full compliance with privacy regulations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Data Modality Mapping</h5>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The synthetic dataset’s geometric patterns visualized in Figure <a href="#S6.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ Validation Framework ‣ 6.1.3 Federated Data Partitioning Strategy ‣ 6.1 Synthetic Multi-View Data Generation Framework ‣ 6 Experimental Evaluation ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> serve as proxies for real medical data characteristics:</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">View 1 (Physiological Measurements):</span> The four distinct shapes in View 1 represent different patient populations based on physiological measurements:</p>
<ul id="S6.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S6.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Circular cluster:</span> Represents healthy control patients with normal, tightly distributed physiological parameters</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Elliptical cluster:</span> Models patients with mild cardiovascular risk showing elongated parameter distributions</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Crescent cluster:</span> Captures patients with complex, non-linear disease progression patterns</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I5.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I5.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I5.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I5.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Spiral cluster:</span> Represents patients with progressive disease states showing temporal evolution</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">View 2 (Imaging and Behavioral Data):</span> The complementary shapes in View 2 correspond to imaging and behavioral characteristics:</p>
<ul id="S6.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S6.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Diamond cluster:</span> Structured imaging features with clear anatomical boundaries</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I6.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ring cluster:</span> Patients with preserved central function but peripheral abnormalities</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I6.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cross cluster:</span> Behavioral patterns showing distinct lifestyle factor combinations</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I6.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I6.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I6.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I6.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Heart cluster:</span> Complex cardiac structural abnormalities requiring specialized interpretation</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Privacy-Preserving Collaborative Analysis</h5>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this medical federated scenario, Hospital A (with 8,500 patient records) and Hospital B (with 1,500 patient records) implement FedHK-MVFC to achieve several clinical objectives:</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="S6.I7" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S6.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I7.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Enhanced Statistical Power:</span> By collaborating, hospitals achieve the statistical power necessary for robust phenotype identification that would be impossible with individual datasets</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S6.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I7.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cross-Population Validation:</span> Different patient populations across hospitals enable validation of phenotyping models across diverse demographic and geographic contexts</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S6.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I7.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rare Disease Detection:</span> Collaborative analysis improves detection of rare cardiovascular phenotypes that may be underrepresented in individual hospital datasets</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I7.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S6.I7.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I7.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I7.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Treatment Protocol Harmonization:</span> Consistent phenotyping across institutions enables standardized treatment protocols and outcome comparison</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Clinical Workflow Implementation</h5>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The FedHK-MVFC implementation in this medical scenario follows a structured clinical workflow:</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Phase 1 - Local Data Preparation:</span>
Each hospital preprocesses their local patient data, ensuring data quality and consistency while computing heat-kernel coefficients that capture the intrinsic geometry of their patient populations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Phase 2 - Federated Model Training:</span>
Hospitals iteratively update their local clustering models using FedHK-MVFC while sharing only aggregated model parameters (cluster centers, view weights) with the federated server. No raw patient data is transmitted.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Phase 3 - Collaborative Phenotype Refinement:</span>
The global model aggregation enables each hospital to refine their patient phenotypes based on collective knowledge while maintaining personalized adjustments for their specific patient population.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Phase 4 - Clinical Validation and Deployment:</span>
The resulting patient phenotypes are validated against clinical outcomes and integrated into electronic health record systems for clinical decision support.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This medical scenario demonstrates how the geometric complexity of our synthetic dataset translates to real-world medical applications where FedHK-MVFC enables privacy-preserving collaborative analysis that enhances clinical decision-making while respecting patient privacy and institutional autonomy. This medical federated scenario is visualized in Figure <a href="#S6.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Federated Data Distribution Analysis ‣ 6.1.4 Medical Federated Scenario: Multi-Hospital Patient Data Analysis ‣ 6.1 Synthetic Multi-View Data Generation Framework ‣ 6 Experimental Evaluation ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, which illustrates the complete workflow from data preparation through federated model training to clinical phenotype identification.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Scenario Description</h5>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Take the generated synthetic dataset as a basis for our medical scenario. Consider two major hospitals, Hospital A and Hospital B, seeking to collaboratively analyze patient cardiovascular health patterns without sharing sensitive medical data. Each hospital has collected multi-modal patient data over several years:</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="S6.I8" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S6.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I8.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I8.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hospital A (Client 1):</span> Large metropolitan hospital with 8,500 patient records</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I8.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I8.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hospital B (Client 2):</span> Specialized cardiac center with 1,500 patient records</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Multi-View Medical Data Structure</h5>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each patient record consists of two complementary views capturing different aspects of cardiovascular health:</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">View 1 - Physiological Measurements:</span></p>
<ul id="S6.I9" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S6.I9.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I9.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I9.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">ECG-derived features (heart rate variability, QT intervals)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I9.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I9.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I9.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Blood pressure patterns (systolic/diastolic variations)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I9.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I9.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I9.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Laboratory biomarkers (troponin levels, cholesterol profiles)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I9.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I9.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I9.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Physical examination metrics (BMI, pulse characteristics)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">View 2 - Imaging and Behavioral Data:</span></p>
<ul id="S6.I10" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S6.I10.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I10.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I10.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Cardiac MRI-derived structural features (ventricular volumes, wall thickness)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I10.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I10.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I10.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Echocardiogram functional parameters (ejection fraction, valve performance)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I10.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I10.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I10.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Lifestyle and behavioral indicators (exercise capacity, medication adherence)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I10.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I10.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I10.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Risk factor profiles (family history, smoking status, comorbidities)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Clustering Objectives</h5>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The collaborative analysis aims to identify four distinct patient phenotypes:</p>
<ol id="S6.I11" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I11.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S6.I11.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I11.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I11.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Healthy Controls:</span> Patients with normal cardiovascular function across all modalities</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I11.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S6.I11.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I11.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I11.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Early-Stage Risk:</span> Patients showing subtle abnormalities requiring preventive intervention</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I11.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S6.I11.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I11.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I11.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Moderate Disease:</span> Patients with established cardiovascular conditions requiring active management</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I11.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S6.I11.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I11.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I11.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Severe/Complex Cases:</span> Patients with advanced disease requiring specialized care protocols</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px8" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Privacy and Compliance Requirements</h5>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The federated learning approach addresses critical healthcare constraints:</p>
<ul id="S6.I12" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S6.I12.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I12.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I12.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I12.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">HIPAA Compliance:</span> Patient data never leaves the originating hospital</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I12.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I12.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I12.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I12.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Institutional Policies:</span> Each hospital maintains full control over their data access</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I12.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I12.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I12.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I12.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Regulatory Requirements:</span> All analysis meets medical research ethics standards</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I12.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I12.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I12.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I12.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Clinical Utility:</span> Results must be interpretable for medical decision-making</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px9" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Federated Data Distribution Analysis</h5>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To provide further insights into the federated learning scenario, Figure <a href="#S6.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ Federated Data Distribution Analysis ‣ 6.1.4 Medical Federated Scenario: Multi-Hospital Patient Data Analysis ‣ 6.1 Synthetic Multi-View Data Generation Framework ‣ 6 Experimental Evaluation ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> presents a comprehensive visualization of the data distribution across the two hospitals. This visualization demonstrates how the synthetic multi-view dataset is partitioned in a realistic federated healthcare setting, where different institutions contribute varying amounts of data while maintaining the same underlying patient phenotype structure.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px9.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px9.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The data distribution analysis reveals several important characteristics of the federated scenario:</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px9.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="S6.I13" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S6.I13.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I13.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I13.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I13.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Heterogeneous Sample Sizes:</span> Hospital A contributes 85% of the total data (8,500 records) while Hospital B contributes 15% (1,500 records), reflecting realistic differences in hospital capacity and patient volume</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I13.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I13.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I13.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I13.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Consistent Phenotype Representation:</span> Both hospitals maintain representation of all four patient phenotypes, ensuring that federated learning can identify global patterns</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I13.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I13.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I13.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I13.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">View Complementarity Preservation:</span> The geometric complexity and complementary nature of the two views are maintained across both hospital datasets</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I13.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I13.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I13.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I13.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Statistical Representativeness:</span> Despite different sample sizes, both hospitals capture the essential statistical properties of each patient phenotype</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="S6.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S6.F2.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.15844v1/images/client1_view1.png" id="S6.F2.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/357;" width="476" height="357" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Hospital A (Client 1) - View 1: ECG-derived features, Blood pressure trends, Laboratory biomarkers, and Physical examination metrics (8,500 patient records)</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S6.F2.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.15844v1/images/client1_view2.png" id="S6.F2.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/357;" width="476" height="357" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Hospital A (Client 1) - View 2: Cardiac MRI structural characteristics, Echocardiogram functional details, Lifestyle and behavioral factors, and Risk factor profiles (8,500 patient records)</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S6.F2.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.15844v1/images/client2_view1.png" id="S6.F2.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/357;" width="476" height="357" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>Hospital B (Client 2) - View 1: ECG-derived features, Blood pressure trends, Laboratory biomarkers, and Physical examination metrics (1,500 patient records)</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S6.F2.sf4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.15844v1/images/client2_view2.png" id="S6.F2.sf4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/357;" width="476" height="357" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(d) </span>Hospital B (Client 2) - View 2: Cardiac MRI structural characteristics, Echocardiogram functional details, Lifestyle and behavioral factors, and Risk factor profiles (1,500 patient records)</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>Multi-view federated clustering visualization showing data distribution across two hospitals. Hospital A (Client 1) contributes 8,500 patient records while Hospital B (Client 2) contributes 1,500 patient records. Each hospital provides two complementary views: View 1 contains physiological measurements (ECG features, blood pressure, laboratory biomarkers, physical examination), while View 2 encompasses imaging and behavioral data (cardiac MRI, echocardiogram, lifestyle factors, risk profiles). The federated learning framework enables collaborative patient phenotyping while preserving data privacy across institutions.</figcaption>
</figure>
