<span id="S6.F3.7.1.1.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.F3.7.1.1.2.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1,500</span></span>
<span id="S6.F3.7.1.1.2.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.F3.7.1.1.2.6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">10,000 patients</span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span>
<span id="S6.F3.7.1.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S6.F3.7.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Privacy Preserved:</span> No raw patient data exchanged</span>
<span id="S6.F3.7.1.3" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S6.F3.7.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Clinical Utility:</span> Enhanced phenotyping accuracy through multi-hospital collaboration</span>
<span id="S6.F3.7.1.4" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S6.F3.7.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Regulatory Compliance:</span> HIPAA-compliant federated learning protocol</span>
</span></p></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Medical Federated Scenario: Multi-Hospital Cardiovascular Patient Analysis using FedHK-MVFC. Hospital A (8,500 records) and Hospital B (1,500 records) collaborate to identify patient phenotypes while preserving data privacy. The heat-kernel enhanced framework enables effective clustering across complementary medical views (physiological measurements and imaging/behavioral data) without sharing sensitive patient information.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px10" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">FedHK-MVFC Advantages in Medical Applications</h5>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The heat-kernel enhanced approach provides several key advantages for medical federated learning:</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px10.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="S6.I14" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I14.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S6.I14.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I14.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I14.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Geometry-Aware Similarity:</span> Heat-kernel coefficients capture the intrinsic manifold structure of medical data, accounting for the non-linear relationships between physiological parameters</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I14.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S6.I14.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I14.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I14.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Multi-Modal Integration:</span> The framework naturally handles heterogeneous medical data types (continuous lab values, discrete imaging features, categorical risk factors)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I14.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S6.I14.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I14.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I14.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Privacy Preservation:</span> Only anonymized model parameters are shared, ensuring compliance with healthcare privacy regulations</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I14.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S6.I14.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I14.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I14.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Clinical Interpretability:</span> The clustering results provide clinically meaningful patient phenotypes that align with established medical knowledge</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I14.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="S6.I14.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I14.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I14.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Robustness to Data Heterogeneity:</span> The algorithm handles different patient populations and measurement protocols across hospitals</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px10.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS4.Px10.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This medical scenario demonstrates how the synthetic data experiments (with their controlled geometric complexities) translate to real-world healthcare applications where FedHK-MVFC can enable privacy-preserving collaborative analysis across medical institutions.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.2 </span>Real-World Case Study: A Benchmark Dataset</h3>

<div id="S6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Iris dataset is a classic benchmark in machine learning, consisting of 150 samples of iris flowers with four features: sepal length, sepal width, petal length, and petal width. In this case study, we apply the FedHK-MVFC framework to the Iris dataset, simulating a federated learning environment with two clients. The dataset is partitioned such that each client holds a subset of the data, and we aim to cluster the samples into three species: Iris Setosa, Iris Versicolor, and Iris Virginica.
We first create a scenario on Iris dataset where attributes 1 and 3 are used for View 1, and attributes 2 and 4 are used for View 2. Then, we distribute the data points between the two clients while ensuring that both views are represented. Each client has access to all three species, but the distribution of samples is uneven, simulating a realistic federated learning scenario. Client one holds 90 samples, while client two holds 60 samples.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.3 </span>Experimental Setup and Evaluation Metrics</h3>

<section id="S6.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.3.1 </span>Baseline Algorithms</h4>

<div id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare our proposed HK-MVFC and FedHK-MVFC algorithms against state-of-the-art multi-view clustering methods:</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="S6.I15" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S6.I15.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I15.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I15.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I15.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Multi-View Fuzzy C-Means (MV-FCM)</span>: Traditional extension of FCM to multi-view data</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I15.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I15.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I15.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I15.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Co-regularized Multi-View Spectral Clustering (CoMSC)</span>: Spectral approach with cross-view regularization</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I15.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I15.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I15.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I15.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Federated Multi-View K-Means (FedMV-KMeans)</span>: Federated extension of multi-view k-means</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I15.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I15.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I15.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I15.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Multi-View Deep Clustering (MVDC)</span>: Deep learning-based multi-view clustering</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.3.2 </span>Evaluation Metrics</h4>

<div id="S6.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Clustering performance is assessed using multiple complementary metrics:</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS3.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Accuracy-based Metrics:</h5>

<div id="S6.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S6.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E116"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S6.E116.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Accuracy</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E116.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{I}[\hat{y}_{i}=y_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{I}[\hat{y}_{i}=y_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(116)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E117"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S6.E117.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Normalized Mutual Information (NMI)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E117.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{2\cdot\text{MI}(\mathbf{y},\hat{\mathbf{y}})}{\text{H}(\mathbf{y})+\text{H}(\hat{\mathbf{y}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>MI</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>H</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>H</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{2\cdot\text{MI}(\mathbf{y},\hat{\mathbf{y}})}{\text{H}(\mathbf{y})+\text{H}(\hat{\mathbf{y}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(117)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E118"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S6.E118.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Adjusted Rand Index (ARI)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E118.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\text{RI}-\mathbb{E}[\text{RI}]}{\max(\text{RI})-\mathbb{E}[\text{RI}]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mtext>RI</mtext><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtext>RI</mtext><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>RI</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtext>RI</mtext><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\text{RI}-\mathbb{E}[\text{RI}]}{\max(\text{RI})-\mathbb{E}[\text{RI}]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(118)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Geometric Fidelity Metrics:</h5>

<div id="S6.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S6.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E119"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S6.E119.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Silhouette Coefficient</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E119.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{b_{i}-a_{i}}{\max(a_{i},b_{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{b_{i}-a_{i}}{\max(a_{i},b_{i})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(119)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E120"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S6.E120.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Calinski-Harabasz Index</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E120.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\text{SSB}/(\text{c}-1)}{\text{SSW}/(\text{N}-\text{c})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mtext>SSB</mtext><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>c</mtext><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mtext>SSW</mtext><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>N</mtext><mo>−</mo><mtext>c</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\text{SSB}/(\text{c}-1)}{\text{SSW}/(\text{N}-\text{c})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(120)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3.SSS2.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Multi-View Specific Metrics:</h5>

<div id="S6.SS3.SSS2.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S6.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E121"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S6.E121.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">View Consensus</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E121.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{S}\sum_{h=1}^{S}\text{NMI}(\hat{\mathbf{y}},\hat{\mathbf{y}}^{(h)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mtext>NMI</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{S}\sum_{h=1}^{S}\text{NMI}(\hat{\mathbf{y}},\hat{\mathbf{y}}^{(h)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(121)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E122"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S6.E122.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Cross-View Stability</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E122.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\frac{1}{S(S-1)}\sum_{h\neq h^{\prime}}\|\mathbf{V}^{(h)}-\mathbf{V}^{(h^{\prime})}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\frac{1}{S(S-1)}\sum_{h\neq h^{\prime}}\|\mathbf{V}^{(h)}-\mathbf{V}^{(h^{\prime})}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(122)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.3.3 </span>Computational Complexity Analysis</h4>

<div id="S6.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The synthetic data generation framework exhibits the following computational complexities:</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS3.SSS3.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Data Generation Complexity:</h5>

<div id="S6.SS3.SSS3.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS3.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For generating <math id="S6.SS3.SSS3.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> samples across <math id="S6.SS3.SSS3.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> views with <math id="S6.SS3.SSS3.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> clusters:</p>
<table id="S6.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E123"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{O}_{generation}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{O}_{generation}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E123.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{O}(N\cdot S\cdot C_{shape})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{O}(N\cdot S\cdot C_{shape})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(123)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E124"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{O}_{validation}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{O}_{validation}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E124.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{O}(N\cdot S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{O}(N\cdot S)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(124)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E125"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{O}_{total}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{O}_{total}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E125.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{O}(N\cdot S\cdot(C_{shape}+1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{O}(N\cdot S\cdot(C_{shape}+1))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(125)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS3.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS3.SSS3.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{shape}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{shape}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the computational cost of the most complex shape generation (heart curve: <math id="S6.SS3.SSS3.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> per sample).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3.SSS3.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Federated Partitioning Complexity:</h5>

<div id="S6.SS3.SSS3.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S6.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E126"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{O}_{partition}=\mathcal{O}(N\log N+P\cdot N/P)=\mathcal{O}(N\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{O}_{partition}=\mathcal{O}(N\log N+P\cdot N/P)=\mathcal{O}(N\log N)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(126)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS3.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS3.SSS3.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of federated clients.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.3.4 </span>Theoretical Properties of the Synthetic Framework</h4>

<section id="S6.SS3.SSS4.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Geometric Diversity Theorem:</h5>

<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Geometric Coverage)<span id="Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}=\{G_{1},G_{2},\ldots,G_{C}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}=\{G_{1},G_{2},\ldots,G_{C}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of geometric shapes in our synthetic framework. The framework provides complete coverage of fundamental topological properties:</span></p>
<table id="S6.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E127"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bigcup_{i=1}^{C}\text{Hull}(G_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Hull</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigcup_{i=1}^{C}\text{Hull}(G_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E127.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\supset\{\text{convex, non-convex, simply-connected, multiply-connected}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⊃</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">convex, non-convex, simply-connected, multiply-connected</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\supset\{\text{convex, non-convex, simply-connected, multiply-connected}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(127)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E128"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bigcup_{i=1}^{C}\text{Curvature}(G_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Curvature</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigcup_{i=1}^{C}\text{Curvature}(G_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E128.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\supset\{0,+\kappa,-\kappa,\text{variable}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⊃</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">variable</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\supset\{0,+\kappa,-\kappa,\text{variable}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(128)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3.SSS4.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">View Complementarity Property:</h5>

<div id="Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Cross-View Information Content)<span id="Thmproposition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any two views <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}^{(h)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}^{(h)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}^{(h^{\prime})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}^{(h^{\prime})}</annotation></semantics></math> in our synthetic framework:</span></p>
<table id="S6.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E129"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{MI}(\mathbf{X}^{(h)},\mathbf{X}^{(h^{\prime})})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">MI</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{MI}(\mathbf{X}^{(h)},\mathbf{X}^{(h^{\prime})})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E129.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 0.7\cdot\max(\text{H}(\mathbf{X}^{(h)}),\text{H}(\mathbf{X}^{(h^{\prime})}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>0.7</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">H</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">H</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 0.7\cdot\max(\text{H}(\mathbf{X}^{(h)}),\text{H}(\mathbf{X}^{(h^{\prime})}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(129)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E130"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{MI}(y^{(h)},y^{(h^{\prime})})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">MI</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{MI}(y^{(h)},y^{(h^{\prime})})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E130.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 0.8\cdot\text{H}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">H</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 0.8\cdot\text{H}(y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(130)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">ensuring that views provide complementary features while maintaining consistent cluster structure.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3.SSS5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.3.5 </span>Statistical Validation Framework</h4>

<div id="S6.SS3.SSS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure the reliability and reproducibility of our synthetic data generation, we implement a comprehensive statistical validation framework:</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS3.SSS5.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Shape Fidelity Validation:</h5>

<div id="S6.SS3.SSS5.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS5.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each generated cluster <math id="S6.SS3.SSS5.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, we verify:</p>
<table id="S6.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E131"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S6.E131.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Hausdorff Distance:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E131.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{H}(\mathcal{C}_{k},\mathcal{T}_{k})\leq\epsilon_{shape}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{H}(\mathcal{C}_{k},\mathcal{T}_{k})\leq\epsilon_{shape}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(131)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E132"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S6.E132.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Frechet Distance:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E132.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{F}(\mathcal{C}_{k},\mathcal{T}_{k})\leq\epsilon_{curve}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{F}(\mathcal{C}_{k},\mathcal{T}_{k})\leq\epsilon_{curve}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(132)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E133"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S6.E133.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Sample Count Validation:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E133.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\mathcal{C}_{k}|=N_{c}\pm 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>±</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\mathcal{C}_{k}|=N_{c}\pm 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(133)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS5.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS3.SSS5.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the theoretical shape template, <math id="S6.SS3.SSS5.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{shape}=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{shape}=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S6.SS3.SSS5.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{curve}=0.15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{curve}=0.15</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3.SSS5.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Statistical Distribution Testing:</h5>

<div id="S6.SS3.SSS5.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS5.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We apply multiple statistical tests to validate the generated data:</p>
<ul id="S6.I16" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S6.I16.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I16.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I16.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I16.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Kolmogorov-Smirnov test</span> for noise distribution verification</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I16.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I16.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I16.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I16.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Anderson-Darling test</span> for parametric distribution validation</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I16.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I16.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I16.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I16.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Shapiro-Wilk test</span> for Gaussian noise components</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I16.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I16.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I16.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I16.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Chi-square test</span> for uniform angular distributions</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.SSS5.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS5.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">All tests are performed with significance level <math id="S6.SS3.SSS5.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, and datasets failing any test are regenerated.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.4 </span>Results and Discussion</h3>

<section id="S6.SS4.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.4.1 </span>Performance on Synthetic Multi-View Data</h4>

<div id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S6.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 6.4.1 Performance on Synthetic Multi-View Data ‣ 6.4 Results and Discussion ‣ 6 Experimental Evaluation ‣ FedHK-MVFC: Federated Heat Kernel Multi-View Clustering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> presents comprehensive performance comparison on our synthetic multi-view dataset. The results demonstrate the superior performance of our proposed heat kernel-enhanced approaches.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Performance Comparison on Synthetic Multi-View Data</figcaption>
<table id="S6.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S6.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm</span></th>
<td id="S6.T2.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Accuracy</span></td>
<td id="S6.T2.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T2.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NMI</span></td>
<td id="S6.T2.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T2.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ARI</span></td>
<td id="S6.T2.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T2.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Silhouette</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T2.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T2.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">MV-FCM</th>
<td id="S6.T2.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">0.743</td>
<td id="S6.T2.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">0.682</td>
<td id="S6.T2.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">0.651</td>
<td id="S6.T2.2.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">0.421</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T2.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T2.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">CoMSC</th>
<td id="S6.T2.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">0.768</td>
